  0%|          | 0/500 [00:00<?, ?it/s]['yes'] {'response': 'Yes, both Joseph Roth and Cid Corman were authors. Cid Corman was an American poet, translator, and editor, known for his significant contributions to American poetry in the second half of the 20th century, particularly through his work with "Origin." Joseph Roth, although not mentioned directly in the context provided, is implied to be an author due to the mention of publications of his works in the 21st century, which indicates that he wrote literary works that have been published and revived interest in his contributions. Therefore, it can be concluded that both individuals were indeed authors in their respective fields.', 'query': 'Were both Joseph Roth and Cid Corman authors?', 'retrieved_context': [{'text': 'Cid (Sidney) Corman (June 29, 1924 – March 12, 2004) was an American poet, translator and editor, most notably of "Origin", who was a key figure in the history of American poetry in the second half of the 20th century.', 'node_id': '27e3b31f-c67c-4fa9-9ff1-330227226120', 'score': 0.8194947838783264}, {'text': 'Theodore Vernon Enslin (born March 25, 1925 – November 21, 2011) was an American poet associated with Cid Corman\'s "Origin" and press. He is widely regarded as one of the most musical of American avant-garde poets.', 'node_id': '90ab5b96-41bf-4da1-bcb1-791a2ef94acb', 'score': 1.0509424209594727}, {'text': 'In the 21st century, publications in English of "Radetzky March" and of collections of his journalism from Berlin and Paris created a revival of interest in Roth.', 'node_id': '5852e876-abd0-4e0b-b6d9-13794452f6d7', 'score': 1.052304983139038}, {'text': 'Meyer Levin (October 7, 1905 – July 9, 1981) was an American novelist. Perhaps best known for his work on the Leopold and Loeb case, Levin worked as a journalist (for the "Chicago Daily News" and, from 1933–39, as an editor for "Esquire").', 'node_id': 'a39095f8-287b-4785-ae76-faaed4066632', 'score': 1.0953218936920166}, {'text': 'Joseph Hillis Miller Jr. (born March 5, 1928) is an American literary critic who has been heavily influenced by—and who has heavily influenced—deconstruction.', 'node_id': '5b687bf6-31e5-4fdd-a8ea-97b4f9e970ed', 'score': 1.1113502979278564}], 'consistency_check': 'MISSING', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'NEUTRAL', 'response': 'ENTAILMENT'}, 'latency': 2.9225272610783577, 'vram_usage': 1.14208984375}
