['Chicago'] {'response': 'The provided context is insufficient regarding Axle Whitehead\'s involvement in the series "Shameless." However, it does mention that "Shameless" is set in Chicago.', 'query': 'Axle Whitehead was a part of an American comedy-drama television series that is a remake of the British series with the same name set in what city?', 'retrieved_context': [{'text': 'Shameless is an American comedy-drama television series which airs on Showtime. It is the remake of the British series of the same name. Set in Chicago, the series is filmed in Los Angeles, with the exterior scenes shot in Chicago.', 'node_id': '26182131-2773-463b-b817-02a844872c64', 'score': 18.491252899169922}, {'text': 'The eighth season of "Shameless", an American comedy-drama television series based on the award-winning British series of the same name by Paul Abbott, was announced on December 19, 2016, a day after the seventh season finale. The season will consist of a total of 12 episodes. It is slated to premiere on November 5, 2017.', 'node_id': 'dafebd4f-fb9b-4921-bc49-d7447e0f3db9', 'score': 11.805853843688965}, {'text': 'The fifth season of "Shameless", an American comedy-drama television series based on the award-winning British series of the same name by Paul Abbott, premiered on January 11, 2015 on the Showtime television network. Executive producers are John Wells, Paul Abbott and Andrew Stearn, and producer Michael Hissrich. Like all previous seasons, the season consisted of 12 episodes.', 'node_id': '9e3c05da-81a2-457c-91be-a0f860d46192', 'score': 11.354301452636719}, {'text': 'The first season of "Shameless", an American comedy-drama television series based on the award-winning British series of the same name by Paul Abbott, premiered on January 9, 2011, at Sunday 10:00\xa0p.m. EST on the Showtime television network. Executive producers are John Wells, Paul Abbott and Andrew Stearn, with producer Michael Hissrich. The season concluded after 12 episodes on March 27, 2011.', 'node_id': '2d3b9fbd-aa06-4678-989f-9223c1f333e2', 'score': 11.040092468261719}, {'text': 'The fourth season episode 10 of "Shameless", an American comedy-drama television series based on the award-winning British series of the same name by Paul Abbott, premiered on January 12, 2014, at Sunday 9:00\xa0p.m. EST on the Showtime television network. Executive producers are John Wells, Paul Abbott and Andrew Stearn, with producer Michael Hissrich. The season concluded after 12 episodes on April 6, 2014.', 'node_id': '5b56e983-cdaf-43a8-ac04-eb1a6ea7a2b6', 'score': 10.939271926879883}, {'text': 'The sixth season of "Shameless", an American comedy-drama television series based on the award-winning British series of the same name by Paul Abbott, premiered on January 10, 2016, concluded April 3, 2016. Executive producers are John Wells, Andrew Stearn, Nancy M. Pimental, Davey Holmes, Christopher Chulack, Krista Vernoff and producers Terri Murphy and Princess Nash.', 'node_id': '57a79760-c0cc-413c-97b7-fa06db35e74f', 'score': 10.871088027954102}, {'text': 'The seventh season of "Shameless", based on the award-winning British series of the same name by Paul Abbott, is an American comedy-drama television series with executive producers John Wells, Christopher Chulack, Krista Vernoff, Etan Frankel, Nancy M. Pimental and Sheila Callaghan. The season premiered on October 2, 2016, the first time the series has debuted in autumn. Showtime premiered a free preview of the season premiere online on September 23, 2016, ahead of the October 2 broadcast.', 'node_id': '0f79c3f7-43b0-4520-a9d9-63e46b63687e', 'score': 10.313668251037598}, {'text': 'The second season of "Shameless", an American comedy-drama television series based on the award-winning British series of the same name by Paul Abbott, premiered on January 8, 2012, at Sunday 9:00\xa0p.m. EST on the Showtime television network. Executive producers are John Wells, Paul Abbott and Andrew Stearn, with producer Michael Hissrich. The season concluded after 12 episodes on April 1, 2012. The shows season premiere brought in 1.58 million viewers, which was higher than the season 1 premiere.', 'node_id': '8ba3e9d5-6cbd-4005-adf0-95a22c535ae7', 'score': 10.109939575195312}, {'text': 'The third season of "Shameless", an American comedy-drama television series based on the award-winning British series of the same name by Paul Abbott, premiered on January 13, 2013, at Sunday 9:00\xa0p.m. EST on the Showtime television network. Executive producers are John Wells, Paul Abbott and Andrew Stearn, with producer Michael Hissrich. The season concluded after 12 episodes on April 7, 2013. The shows season premiere brought in 2.00 million viewers, becoming the show highest rated episode ever to-date.', 'node_id': 'b057be01-74ea-44b1-8d42-05eec21fb061', 'score': 9.861258506774902}, {'text': 'When "Part 2" aired, it set a series high and a new viewership record for the most watched episode of a regular drama series ever in basic cable with 9.4 million viewers. Both parts were written by series creator Andy Breckman and directed by Randall Zisk.', 'node_id': 'f0def9d7-4c27-4560-85d2-56a5f768349e', 'score': 8.725777626037598}], 'consistency_check': 'MISSING', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'NEUTRAL', 'response': 'ENTAILMENT'}, 'latency': 5.356822503730655, 'vram_usage': 0.0}
