['I-90'] {'response': 'New York State Route 890 (NY 890) runs through Schenectady, New York, alongside Route 146 and Interstate 890 (I-890). Additionally, New York State Route 337 (NY 337) also runs through Schenectady, as it forms a connection from NY 7 to Interstate 890 along the western edge of the city. Therefore, the three highways that run through Schenectady are Route 146, Interstate 890, and Route 337.', 'query': 'Route 146, Interstate 890, and what other highway all run through Schenectady, New York?', 'retrieved_context': [{'text': 'Interstate 890 (I-890) is a 9.45 mi long auxiliary Interstate Highway in the vicinity of Schenectady, New York, in the United States. The highway runs southeast–northwest from an interchange with the New York State Thruway (I-90) northwest of Schenectady to another junction with the Thruway south of the city and passes through Downtown Schenectady along the way. Most of I-890 is six lanes wide, including a section that runs above an industrial section of Schenectady on an elevated highway.', 'node_id': '8e3e528b-d578-4bb5-9bf9-d1de4a6b246d', 'score': 20.946701049804688}, {'text': 'New York State Route\xa0890 (NY\xa0890) is a 1.00 mi long state highway located northwest of downtown Schenectady in the Capital District of New York in the United States. Although the route runs north–south, it is signed as east–west to match the posted direction of Interstate\xa0890 (I-890), of which NY\xa0890 is an extension.', 'node_id': '3e84908a-8a1f-4853-8cc4-d0828a61816b', 'score': 19.740825653076172}, {'text': 'New York State Route\xa0337 (NY\xa0337) is a short state highway located entirely within the Town of Rotterdam in Schenectady County, New York. It forms a connection from NY\xa07 to Interstate\xa0890 along the western edge of the city of Schenectady and passes by the Rotterdam Square shopping mall.', 'node_id': 'b317d09d-2624-40d2-8871-dce47736eaa0', 'score': 16.84347915649414}, {'text': 'Fort Hunter is a hamlet in the town of Guilderland, New York. Fort Hunter lies along New York Route 146 near the Albany-Schenectady county line. Exit 25 of the Governor Thomas E. Dewey Thruway and exit 9B of Interstate 890 is at the northern limits of the hamlet.', 'node_id': 'eef0a318-48a0-4f02-8873-a530ad72a43b', 'score': 16.633255004882812}, {'text': 'New York State Route\xa0146 (NY\xa0146) is a state highway in the Capital District of New York in the United States. It extends for 43 mi from Gallupville at NY\xa0443 to near Mechanicville at U.S. Route\xa04 (US\xa04) and NY\xa032. NY\xa0146 is a major thoroughfare in the city of Schenectady, just outside Albany.', 'node_id': '8eedb8f5-4d96-4a1f-ae6b-3a49bbe02019', 'score': 15.222149848937988}, {'text': 'New York State Route\xa0146A (NY\xa0146A) is a state highway in New York State. It begins at NY\xa0146 in Clifton Park and ends at NY\xa050 in Ballston Lake. It is located entirely within Saratoga County. Route\xa0146A is the last existing spur of NY\xa0146 in Saratoga and Schenectady counties.', 'node_id': '8eeeef27-fc45-4747-9a4f-ac18fecda8bf', 'score': 14.628108024597168}, {'text': 'Bridge 8, known locally as the Rexford Bridge, is a two-lane bridge crossing the Mohawk River (Erie Canal) northeast of the city of Schenectady in New York, United States. It carries New York State Route\xa0146 (NY\xa0146) from Schenectady County to Rexford, a hamlet in the Saratoga County town of Clifton Park. The bridge was designed by the New York State Department of Public Works and opened in 1965. It has a total length of 727 ft and a main span of 266 ft .', 'node_id': 'a4dad597-1cb9-49fc-be59-4e2219ddb4f1', 'score': 11.440544128417969}, {'text': 'Route 99, also known as the Woonsocket Industrial Highway, is a numbered state highway running 2.9 mi in Providence County, Rhode Island, United States. The route is a nominally north–south limited-access freeway for its entire length. Route 99 serves Manville and the Highland Industrial Park, providing freeway access to the city of Woonsocket from Rhode Island Route 146, which bypasses the city. The southern terminus of Route 99 is at a partial interchange with Route 146 in Lincoln.', 'node_id': '207951a5-6a6b-43d0-b9f7-ac0c6d15d8b2', 'score': 10.778623580932617}, {'text': 'The western terminus of the route is at an intersection with NY\xa05 in the town of Glenville, and its eastern terminus is at an interchange with I-890 in the town of Rotterdam, where NY\xa0890 becomes I-890 and continues east into Downtown Schenectady.', 'node_id': '23d9a594-fe4a-4805-b1c6-3a66464baf2f', 'score': 10.748226165771484}, {'text': 'Most of the route follows an east–west alignment; however, the middle third of the route between Guilderland and Clifton Park runs in a more north–south manner in order to serve Schenectady. At one time, NY\xa0146 had three spur routes; only one—NY\xa0146A—still exists.', 'node_id': 'ff816004-9019-44c4-916c-fea19425cade', 'score': 10.40400505065918}], 'consistency_check': 'MISSING', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'CONTRADICTION', 'response': 'ENTAILMENT'}, 'latency': 1.2847318351268768, 'vram_usage': 0.0}
