  6%|▌         | 29/500 [05:26<1:35:24, 12.15s/it]  6%|▌         | 30/500 [05:33<1:22:04, 10.48s/it]  6%|▌         | 31/500 [05:36<1:06:16,  8.48s/it]  6%|▋         | 32/500 [05:39<53:27,  6.85s/it]    7%|▋         | 33/500 [05:46<51:36,  6.63s/it]  7%|▋         | 34/500 [05:50<45:36,  5.87s/it]['yes'] {'response': "Yes, both Grasshopper and Sake bomb are types of drinks. The Grasshopper is a sweet, mint-flavored after-dinner drink that is known for its green color, which comes from crème de menthe. It originated at Tujague's in the French Quarter of New Orleans and became popular in the 1950s and 1960s. On the other hand, the Sake bomb, or sake bomber, is a beer cocktail made by pouring sake into a shot glass and dropping it into a glass of beer. Therefore, both drinks fall under the category of alcoholic beverages, each with its unique preparation and flavor profile.", 'query': 'Are Grasshopper and Sake bomb both types of drinks?', 'retrieved_context': [{'text': "A grasshopper is a sweet, mint-flavored, after-dinner drink. The name of the drink derives from its green color, which comes from crème de menthe. The drink reputedly originated at Tujague's, a landmark bar in the French Quarter of New Orleans, Louisiana, and was invented by its owner, Philip Guichet. The drink gained popularity during the 1950s and 1960s throughout the American South.", 'node_id': '63128dac-2338-4412-91fe-3a4ba96e7307', 'score': 0.7761067152023315}, {'text': 'The sake bomb or sake bomber is a beer cocktail made by pouring sake into a shot glass and dropping it into a glass of beer.', 'node_id': 'dcb0b0d6-f9e6-4273-8c6e-a1f73441129a', 'score': 0.8110954761505127}, {'text': 'The products of the company and its subsidiaries include various types of whiskey, vodka, gin, tequila, rum, brandy, cognac, cocktails, cordials, liqueurs, "shooters", and wine.', 'node_id': 'c66f14ad-51a9-4ae1-9b74-a8ff74ec0abf', 'score': 1.1402873992919922}, {'text': 'Tequila and tonic, also known as TnT or Teqtonic, is a non-standard highball beverage. The drink is made with a 2:1 ratio of tonic water to tequila and is served with lemon or lime wedges on ice.', 'node_id': '17af1bf1-1493-493d-90b9-e456f93f5a73', 'score': 1.1535289287567139}, {'text': 'In order to accommodate the places which sell sake and other drinks, Coca-Cola and other soft drink makers have worked to expand the varieties of their products. One way of selling more of their goods is by lining them up next to milk and other products, which helps increase sales at places such as sentō, onsen and convenience stores.', 'node_id': 'ecefcebe-4f7a-4e0c-90c5-551070533fc9', 'score': 1.1937997341156006}], 'consistency_check': 'CONSISTENT', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'NEUTRAL', 'response': 'ENTAILMENT'}, 'latency': 1.2149085495620966, 'vram_usage': 1.15380859375}
