  7%|▋         | 37/500 [06:17<56:40,  7.34s/it]  8%|▊         | 38/500 [06:20<46:48,  6.08s/it]['playwright'] {'response': 'Kōbō Abe and Agatha Christie both share the profession of being writers. Kōbō Abe was a Japanese writer known for his modernist and surreal explorations of individuals in contemporary society, while Agatha Christie was an English crime novelist and playwright, famous for her detective novels and short stories featuring characters like Hercule Poirot and Miss Marple. Both authors have made significant contributions to literature in their respective genres, with Abe often being compared to other modernist writers and Christie being recognized as one of the most prolific and celebrated crime writers in history.', 'query': 'What profession do Kōbō Abe and Agatha Christie share?', 'retrieved_context': [{'text': 'Kōbō Abe (安部 公房 , "Abe Kōbō" ) , pseudonym of Kimifusa Abe (安部 公房 , "Abe Kimifusa" , March 7, 1924 – January 22, 1993) , was a Japanese writer, playwright, photographer and inventor. Abe has been often compared to Franz Kafka and Alberto Moravia for his modernist sensibilities and his surreal, often nightmarish explorations of individuals in contemporary society.', 'node_id': '24b7a29d-cdfe-4611-aa08-d5b068c31757', 'score': 0.9560072422027588}, {'text': "The Agatha Christie Award (アガサ・クリスティー賞 ) is a Japanese literary award established in 2010 in commemoration of the 120th anniversary of Agatha Christie's birth. The award is presented by Hayakawa Publishing Corporation in association with the Agatha Christie Society, which is chaired by Mathew Pritchard, the grandson of Agatha Christie.", 'node_id': '2115fcc4-f5d8-4cf6-89fe-20bf183c5a71', 'score': 1.061553955078125}, {'text': 'Dame Agatha Mary Clarissa Christie, Lady Mallowan, DBE ("née" Miller; 15 September 1890 – 12 January 1976) was an English crime novelist, short story writer and playwright. She is best known for her 66 detective novels and 14 short story collections, particularly those revolving around her fictional detectives Hercule Poirot and Miss Marple. She also wrote the world\'s longest-running play, a murder mystery, "The Mousetrap", and six romances under the name Mary Westmacott.', 'node_id': '4c343ef0-cfd7-4908-bcd7-2f438f6ab6c3', 'score': 1.1499536037445068}, {'text': 'Gregson Edward Bautzer (April 3, 1911 – October 26, 1987) was an American attorney, representing such stars as Ginger Rogers, Ingrid Bergman and Joan Crawford, Kirk Kerkorian, Howard Hughes and William R. Wilkerson.', 'node_id': 'a8f14c5d-2468-4261-947d-f3aef8f83846', 'score': 1.2040499448776245}, {'text': 'Were she replaced Belinda Olsson. Hedberg is married to sports journalist Christian Olsson and is the daughter of professor Bo Hedberg.', 'node_id': 'f71642f4-af59-491a-bb0f-bc6bc7a06898', 'score': 1.2209502458572388}], 'consistency_check': 'CONFLICT', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'CONTRADICTION', 'response': 'ENTAILMENT'}, 'latency': 1.6849414948374033, 'vram_usage': 1.15380859375}
