ca-912a-46b7-9575-aa90dfe13372', 'score': 0.7246410846710205}, {'text': 'The West Rail Line () is one of the MTR lines in Hong Kong, indicated by the colour dark magenta. It was formerly known as the KCR West Rail (九廣西鐵 ). The line connects Hung Hom Station in Kowloon and Tuen Mun Station in Tuen Mun, 35.7\xa0km away, in 37 minutes. The railway runs through the cities of Kowloon, Castle Peak and Tsuen Wan.', 'node_id': '689ef17f-86f4-45b9-9d1e-36bd61a98034', 'score': 0.7652297019958496}, {'text': 'The East Rail was the only railway line of the Kowloon-Canton Railway Corporation (KCRC) before the construction of "KCR West Rail" (now known as West Rail Line).', 'node_id': '612909d2-4b3b-48ef-99a2-97408a1d0e6e', 'score': 0.8438873291015625}, {'text': 'The East Rail Line () is one of eleven railway lines of the Mass Transit Railway (MTR) system in Hong Kong. It used to be one of the three lines of the Kowloon–Canton Railway (KCR) network. It was known as the KCR British Section (九廣鐵路英段) from 1910 to 1996, and the KCR East Rail (九廣東鐵) from 1996 to 2007.', 'node_id': 'af08347e-2e97-47a6-a416-330e7fdb43e0', 'score': 0.8710480332374573}], 'consistency_check': 'CONFLICT', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'ENTAILMENT', 'response': 'ENTAILMENT'}, 'latency': 0.932658139616251, 'vram_usage': 1.39990234375}
