['Richard Ford'] {'response': "The provided context is insufficient regarding Richard Ford's profession or scope of profession to make a comparison with Robert E. Howard. The context only discusses Robert E. Howard's legacy and his most famous character, Conan the Barbarian, along with some associates of PSI and information about Larry Richard Williams. There is no mention of Richard Ford or his professional background.", 'query': 'Who has more scope of profession, Richard Ford or Robert E. Howard?', 'retrieved_context': [{'text': "Robert E. Howard's legacy extended after his death in 1936. Howard's most famous character, Conan the Barbarian, has a pop-culture imprint that has been compared to such icons as Tarzan of the Apes, Count Dracula, Sherlock Holmes, and James Bond. Howard's critical reputation suffered at first but over the decades works of Howard scholarship have been published.", 'node_id': 'bbb23f03-b47d-4576-bdaa-b3720ab68ad0', 'score': -4.984352}, {'text': 'Associates of PSI include: Mathew Atha, Colin Angus, Brian Barritt, Michael Carmichael, Fraser Clark, Paul Devereux, the late John Entwistle, Paul Flynn MP, Ben Ganly, Lee Harris, Mike Jay, Howard Marks, Dr John Marks, Jonathan Ott, Dr Russell Newcombe, Richard Rudgley and Youth.', 'node_id': '68add95d-b361-45c4-8411-11d73be5570e', 'score': -9.734584}, {'text': 'Larry Richard Williams (born October 6, 1942) is an American author, stock and commodity trader, and politician from the state of Montana. He is the father of four-time Academy Award and one-time Tony Award nominee actress Michelle Williams.', 'node_id': 'c4b41d2a-2df5-4592-a717-e52560a54131', 'score': -9.751808}], 'consistency_check': 'CONSISTENT', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'CONTRADICTION', 'response': 'ENTAILMENT'}, 'latency': 1.0851367004215717, 'vram_usage': 10.1279296875}
