 10%|█         | 50/500 [08:36<1:31:24, 12.19s/it]['dancer Gregory Hines'] {'response': 'Maurice Hines and his brother, Gregory Hines, were famous for their contributions to the performing arts, particularly in dance, acting, and music. Maurice Hines is recognized as an actor, director, singer, and choreographer, while Gregory Hines was a renowned dancer and actor. Together, they made significant impacts in the entertainment industry, showcasing their talents in various performances and productions. Their legacy is particularly noted in the realm of tap dancing and musical theater.', 'query': 'Maurice Hines and his brother were famous for what?', 'retrieved_context': [{'text': 'Maurice Hines (born December 13, 1943) is an American actor, director, singer, and choreographer. He is the brother of dancer Gregory Hines.', 'node_id': 'e4b9588b-f124-4965-a724-3ba972740ecb', 'score': 0.42122936248779297}, {'text': "Andrew Hines (born May 25, 1983 in Villa Park, California) is a five-time National Hot Rod Association Pro Stock Motorcycle champion. He rides the flagship Screamin' Eagle/Vance & Hines Harley-Davidson V-rod. Andrew follows in the footsteps of his brother and crew chief, Matt Hines (NHRA Champion 1996, 97, 98). The team is headed by the legendary duo of Terry Vance and Byron Hines.", 'node_id': 'fe8dcb47-cc53-4884-9caa-c7ce280231e4', 'score': 0.8141893148422241}, {'text': 'Guy Thomas "Zeke" Roberts (May 10, 1900 - 1993) was a professional American football player in the early National Football League and the first American Football League. He played for three pro teams over the course of two years. In 1926 he played with the Canton Bulldogs in the NFL and the Cleveland Panthers in the AFL. He played the following season with the NFL\'s Pottsville Maroons. Prior to his professional career, Roberts played college football for the Iowa State Cyclones.', 'node_id': '77102e36-940a-40e1-a8f6-71ae20a61cda', 'score': 1.189135193824768}, {'text': 'Andries Bonger (20 May 1861 – 20 January 1936), nicknamed "Dries", was Johanna van Gogh-Bonger\'s favorite brother. Bonger was a friend of his future brother-in-law Theo van Gogh in Paris. It was through Andries that Johanna and Theo met. He also knew Vincent van Gogh who called him André in letters.', 'node_id': 'cd945815-d3f2-4690-8340-014818f258e4', 'score': 1.1906051635742188}, {'text': "Víctor Manuel Bonilla Hinestroza (born 23 January 1971 in Tumaco) is a retired Colombian striker, more commonly known as 'Big Vic'.", 'node_id': '4cd94bdd-9dc0-48f5-8a8a-a78068e141c5', 'score': 1.2089416980743408}], 'consistency_check': 'CONSISTENT', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'ENTAILMENT', 'response': 'CONTRADICTION'}, 'latency': 1.0152495261281729, 'vram_usage': 1.14208984375}
