30a7a-5981-414f-bc19-3b4b9d4ef108', 'score': 0.9983444213867188}, {'text': 'Over 80% of known desert wildlife species use desert riparian areas. Common dominant species include Fremont cottonwood ("Populus fremontii"), Arizona ash ("Fraxinus velutina"), arroyo willow ("Salix lasiolepis"), Goodding\'s willow ("Salix gooddingii"), red willow ("Salix laevigata"), California fan palm ("Washingtonia filifera"), and invasive species such as salt cedar ("Tamarix ramosissima"), giant reed ("Arundo donax"), and Russian olive ("Elaeagnus angustifolia").', 'node_id': 'af1427e4-5186-47f6-9b0c-fdf22a82aee2', 'score': 1.1326367855072021}], 'consistency_check': 'MISSING', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'ENTAILMENT', 'response': 'NEUTRAL'}, 'latency': 1.0077085066586733, 'vram_usage': 1.24755859375}
