 20%|██        | 101/500 [15:53<1:10:22, 10.58s/it]['is a British author'] {'response': 'The provided context is insufficient regarding the relationship or comparison between Alan Furst and Lee Child.', 'query': 'Alan Furst and Lee Child are what?', 'retrieved_context': [{'text': 'Stuart Lee Murdoch (born 25 August 1968) is a Scottish musician, writer and filmmaker, and the lead singer and songwriter for the indie pop band Belle and Sebastian.', 'node_id': '4f5dbc4f-4bc8-4ce5-810a-7f26f6dc36de', 'score': 1.0901862382888794}, {'text': 'Alan Furst (born February 20, 1941) is an American author of historical spy novels. Furst has been called "an heir to the tradition of Eric Ambler and Graham Greene," whom he cites along with Joseph Roth and Arthur Koestler as important influences. Most of his novels since 1988 have been set just prior to or during the Second World War and he is noted for his successful evocations of Eastern European peoples and places during the period from 1933 to 1944.', 'node_id': 'fcbe1a5a-d516-4133-81cd-f2ede263aff8', 'score': 1.1394379138946533}, {'text': 'As a musician, he has participated in recordings with a-ha, Ray Charles, Ute Lemper, Ian Hunter, Dance with a Stranger, DumDum Boys, Jonas Fjeld Band, Marius Müller, TNT, Arve Tellefsen, Bobbysocks, Bjørn Eidsvåg, Carola Häggkvist and Dee Dee Bridgewater.', 'node_id': '52bf4e26-1342-4b52-aea7-723691bea45e', 'score': 1.2029824256896973}, {'text': 'James Nevin Tait (27 June 1876 – 1961), better known as Nevin Tait, was an Australian concert promoter and film producer born in Castlemaine, Victoria who often collaborated with his brothers Charles and John.', 'node_id': '4ad31047-2467-48a5-bec1-f00d5d312249', 'score': 1.2182872295379639}, {'text': "Senator; Charles Lee, U.S. Supreme Court justice; Richard Bland Lee II, a noted explorer; Robert E. Lee, the Confederate general who is by far the most famous of the family; William Henry Fitzhugh (Rooney) Lee, the son of Robert E. Lee and a U.S. Congressman from Virginia; and Fitzhugh Lee, Governor of Virginia and Civil War cavalry general. President Zachary Taylor was a Lee descendant, on his mother's side.", 'node_id': 'd49aa7f2-b7af-4ed4-a929-4887b1b38337', 'score': 1.223374605178833}], 'consistency_check': 'MISSING', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'CONTRADICTION', 'response': 'NEUTRAL'}, 'latency': 0.628000283613801, 'vram_usage': 1.13037109375}
