 21%|██        | 105/500 [16:39<1:16:04, 11.55s/it]['Orlando'] {'response': 'The provided context is insufficient regarding the specific Florida city that the band Sleeping with Sirens, which released the album "Let\'s Cheers to This," is from.', 'query': 'The band that released the album "Let\'s Cheers to This" is from what Florida city?', 'retrieved_context': [{'text': "Let's Cheers to This is the second studio album by American post-hardcore band Sleeping with Sirens. The album is the first to feature guitarists Jesse Lawson and Jack Fowler.", 'node_id': '6fe613de-22d6-4de6-97cf-f30570ea4424', 'score': 0.8443707227706909}, {'text': 'This album was produced by Simon Says and Jerry Jennings Productions and was recorded at Twelve Note Studio in Fair Oaks, California.', 'node_id': '0da5aedd-a86b-44ff-821c-0650043b06a1', 'score': 1.056058406829834}, {'text': 'The band was signed by Orange Recordings in Los Angeles and toured all over the country, sharing bills with the Demolition Doll Rods, Bob Log III, The Fleshtones, and Immortal Lee County Killers and a one-time show with the Suicide Girls Burlesque Tour in Orlando. While in the Studdogs, Rich Evans began promoting concerts under the tag "Mutiny Productions". He now heads the independent "Florida\'s Dying" label, promoting and releasing material from the Florida-underground music scene.', 'node_id': '1c6637c8-e209-4fc1-ac35-f67431cd8570', 'score': 1.0660333633422852}, {'text': 'Guitarist Jim Fairchild joined the band in 2009. The band\'s sixth album, "Strangers to Ourselves", was released on March 17, 2015.', 'node_id': '18ff4b18-3320-44f1-9c17-5efee72a8fa9', 'score': 1.100619912147522}, {'text': "The University of Florida Fightin' Gator Marching Band, also known as The Pride of the Sunshine, is the official marching band for the University of Florida. They perform at every Florida Gators home football game at Ben Hill Griffin Stadium and also at various other events such as pep rallies, parades, and the annual Orange and Blue spring scrimmage game. A full band usually travels to one away game a year while at other games a small/medium-sized pep band will attend.", 'node_id': '6da6f915-8114-48da-b3be-b22dd2d0a948', 'score': 1.1063892841339111}], 'consistency_check': 'CONSISTENT', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'CONTRADICTION', 'response': 'NEUTRAL'}, 'latency': 0.7106752339750528, 'vram_usage': 1.25927734375}
