['Aleksander Ford'] {'response': 'Aleksander Ford was born first. He was born on November 24, 1908, in Kiev, Russian Empire, while Pablo Trapero was born later on October 4, 1971. Therefore, there is a significant gap of over six decades between their birth dates, with Ford being the earlier of the two.', 'query': 'Who was born first, Pablo Trapero or Aleksander Ford?', 'retrieved_context': [{'text': 'Pablo Trapero (Born 4 October 1971) is an Argentine film producer, editor and director.', 'node_id': '8d5fd586-e48f-4287-8681-e7a44d366f2e', 'score': 0.8675420880317688}, {'text': "Aleksander Ford (born Mosze Lifszyc; 24 November 1908 in Kiev, Russian Empire – 4 April 1980 in Naples, Florida, United States) was a Polish Jewish film director; and head of the Polish People's Army Film Crew in the Soviet Union during World War II. Ford became director of the nationalized Film Polski company following the Red Army occupation of Poland.", 'node_id': '2ae5932e-2ed5-4726-9234-fb8a63a6dadf', 'score': 1.121079444885254}, {'text': 'Born in the U.S.A. is the seventh studio album by American rock singer-songwriter Bruce Springsteen. It was released on June 4, 1984, by Columbia Records. It was written by Springsteen and recorded with his E Street Band and producers Chuck Plotkin and Jon Landau at The Power Station and The Hit Factory in New York City.', 'node_id': 'c64426e7-613a-4316-a12b-1730edc638bf', 'score': 1.1484525203704834}, {'text': 'Sammy Gutiérrez (born 31 December 1985), is a Mexican professional boxer in the Strawweight division. Guty was born in San Martín Texmelucan de Labastida, Puebla, Mexico. On October 23, 2010, he became the interim WBA Minimumweight champion by beating Colombian Luis Carrillo by 3rd round TKO.', 'node_id': 'fabddb8f-f766-4a99-add3-dfc077ac69ae', 'score': 1.1686644554138184}, {'text': 'Austin Young (born April 12, 1966) is an American photographer, film maker and new media artist currently based in Los Angeles. His work has created an encyclopedic documentation of sub and trans culture in New York, Los Angeles and San Francisco.', 'node_id': 'deeeb95d-17ce-491c-a457-48c666633355', 'score': 1.1978461742401123}, {'text': 'Ricardo Del Río Galnares is a film producer born in Mexico City, Mexico. He has co-produced over a dozen U.S. feature films and production managed twice as many international features.', 'node_id': '0fba819b-438b-4b4f-8c90-84fa535095fa', 'score': 1.2021801471710205}, {'text': "Benjamin A. Muncil (28 Aug 1867 – 16 Dec 1930) was an American master builder in the Adirondacks early in the 20th century. He was a major figure in the architectural development of the Adirondack Great Camps; among his many projects was Marjorie Merriweather Post's Camp Topridge, Northbrook Lodge, and White Pine Camp, a summer White House of US President Calvin Coolidge.", 'node_id': '10421482-d982-4352-8174-68e99ac2703b', 'score': 1.2395762205123901}, {'text': "Scott Powell was born in Dallas, Texas, on August 13, 1948. He was a founding member of Sha Na Na, which began at Columbia University in 1969, under the name The Kingsmen. The group's name was later changed to avoid confusion with another band of the same name.", 'node_id': '744ddc6f-a613-4f64-9260-8e0b355fad26', 'score': 1.2485034465789795}, {'text': 'Philip Abramo (born 1945), also known as "The King Of Wall Street", "Lou Metzer" is a caporegime in the New Jersey DeCavalcante crime family who was allegedly involved in security fraud and murder. Abramo was a capo of the DeCavalcante family\'s crew in Miami, Florida.', 'node_id': 'e7a8dadd-d9cd-4a8b-800f-c310c1a9a9d3', 'score': 1.254026174545288}, {'text': 'José Eleazar Gómez Sanchez (] ; better known as Eleazar Gómez born May 29, 1986 in Mexico City, Mexico) is a Mexican actor. He is noted for his performance in Mexican telenovelas. Gómez is the brother of actress Zoraida Gómez and actor Jairo Gómez. He is a member of the Mexican pop band Eme 15.', 'node_id': 'f7f7051c-4219-48df-b35f-2270247692cd', 'score': 1.260127067565918}, {'text': "Davíd Lee Carrasco (born November 21, 1944) is a Mexican-American academic historian of religion, anthropologist, and Mesoamericanist scholar. As of 2001 he holds the inaugural appointment as Neil L. Rudenstine Professor of Latin America Studies at the Harvard Divinity School, in a joint appointment with the Faculty of Arts and Sciences' Department of Anthropology at Harvard University.", 'node_id': 'bf82f13e-c080-4a3d-8790-98ae48e29920', 'score': 1.26715886592865}, {'text': 'George Avakian (Armenian: Գևորգ Ավագյան ; Russian: Геворк Авакян ; born March 15, 1919) is an American record producer and executive known particularly for his work with Columbia Records, and his production of albums by Louis Armstrong, Miles Davis and other notable jazz musicians.', 'node_id': 'c0e035d0-a683-4719-a878-bc4b2d4e58e8', 'score': 1.2675812244415283}, {'text': 'He wrote several works: "Ricaurte en San Mateo", "Niño con Casco", "La misa de los conquistadores", "La Pola conducida al cadalso" and "Reyerta del 20 de julio", among others. He died in Bogota in 1953.', 'node_id': '3cf83fec-6d08-4b4c-bca2-85bdd0182d63', 'score': 1.2706760168075562}, {'text': 'Frank Wolf (born 1970) is a Canadian adventurer, filmmaker, writer and environmentalist. He is known for films, feature magazine articles, and online columns that document wilderness expeditions around the world, with a focus on the Canadian North. His expeditions include being the first to canoe across Canada in one season and cycling 2,000\xa0km in winter on the Yukon River from Dawson to Nome.', 'node_id': 'b69657de-3388-4290-8904-0053e1ebcfb2', 'score': 1.275991439819336}, {'text': 'Mario Fortino Alfonso Moreno Reyes, known casually as Mario Moreno, and known professionally as Cantinflas (August 12, 1911 – April 20, 1993), was a Mexican comic film actor, producer, and screenwriter and an iconic figure in Mexico and Latin America. He often portrayed impoverished "campesinos" or a peasant of "pelado" origin. The character came to be associated with the national identity of Mexico, and allowed Cantinflas to establish a long, successful film career that included a foray into Hollywood.', 'node_id': '4d00002e-2533-42b8-a415-ab0fd5b7c982', 'score': 1.2764618396759033}, {'text': 'During the scene where he helps restore Radiator Springs to its 1950s heyday, he is painted much like a 1950\'s Chevrolet Corvette C1, once again hinting at his Corvette lineage. His number was originally set to be 57, Lasseter\'s birth year, but was changed to 95, the release year of Pixar\'s first film "Toy Story".', 'node_id': '61c39b0c-fe80-4850-ae15-1273d63f919d', 'score': 1.2785102128982544}, {'text': 'He also stopped signing and dating his works so that people would judge his works on their own merit and not by the artist or when they were painted. In 1969, he was made a Companion of the Order of Canada.', 'node_id': '2eef2944-f923-453c-a4b0-a2a0b1f5b727', 'score': 1.2848976850509644}, {'text': 'Nathaniel Robert Bauman (born June 22, 1987 in Petoskey, Michigan) is an American born entertainment consultant and drummer. Currently, he is the drummer for The Band Royale and a monthly contributor for the music publication Modern Drummer. Aside from drumming, he is also known for his development of various start-ups, brands, venues, musicians and athletes.', 'node_id': '37185e95-5492-4f0b-b3d7-224ee79d7684', 'score': 1.2854949235916138}, {'text': 'Douglas Bruce Ford Jr. (born November 20, 1964) is a Canadian businessman and politician in Toronto, Ontario. Ford was Toronto City Councillor for Ward 2 Etobicoke North in Toronto from 2010 to 2014 at the same time that his brother, Rob Ford (1969–2016), was mayor of Toronto. Their father, Doug Ford Sr., was a Member of Provincial Parliament from 1995 to 1999 and founded Deco Labels and Tags, a printing business operating in Canada and the United States.', 'node_id': '0f6b9b53-c5c6-45c4-b16b-df2423430e94', 'score': 1.2882684469223022}, {'text': 'Pedro Alcántara Quijano Montero (1878-1953) was a Colombian artist, engraver, author and set designer. Born in Bogota, he studied at Escuela de Bellas Artes under Recio among others. Later, he taught at his alma mater for more than 30 years. He was also a set designer for the Teatro Colón de Bogotá, and taught several generations of Colombian artists.', 'node_id': 'e97c5ced-0a89-4c65-90c4-5192e3e98619', 'score': 1.2929279804229736}], 'consistency_check': 'CONSISTENT', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'CONTRADICTION', 'response': 'ENTAILMENT'}, 'latency': 0.9923809263855219, 'vram_usage': 1.18896484375}
