producers of Neurofunk (also known more informally as just neuro), which is a subgenre of Drum and Bass as a progression of techstep.", 'node_id': '4ccada00-fe06-4010-9a43-4f9d3a4f2961', 'score': 1.023189902305603}, {'text': 'The band and their producer Nigel Godrich attempted to record it for their albums "OK Computer" (1997), "Kid A" (2000) and "Amnesiac" (2001), but struggled to find an arrangement that satisfied them, and it became one of their most famous unreleased songs. A live recording from the "Amnesiac" tour was released on "" (2001).', 'node_id': '4856a9d1-d10b-48d6-8e6d-db01e828d051', 'score': 1.0253304243087769}], 'consistency_check': 'MISSING', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'CONTRADICTION', 'response': 'NEUTRAL'}, 'latency': 0.7543208934366703, 'vram_usage': 1.25927734375}
