 29%|██▊       | 143/500 [23:48<1:54:11, 19.19s/it]['Saturday Night Live'] {'response': 'The song "Ghostbusters" was written and recorded by Ray Parker Jr. as the theme song for the movie of the same name, which starred Bill Murray, who is a Canadian-American actor and an original member of the Not Ready For Prime Time Players. The show that these cast members were originally associated with is "Saturday Night Live." Therefore, the answer to your question is that "Ghostbusters" is the theme song for a movie starring Bill Murray, who was an original member of the Not Ready For Prime Time Players on "Saturday Night Live."', 'query': 'Ghostbusters is a song written and recorded by Ray Parker Jr. as the theme song for a movie starring a Canadian-American actor who was an original member of the Not Ready for Prime Time Players on what show?', 'retrieved_context': [{'text': '"Ghostbusters" is a song written and recorded by Ray Parker Jr. as the theme to the film of the same name starring Bill Murray, Dan Aykroyd, Harold Ramis, and Ernie Hudson. Debuting at #68 on June 16, 1984, the song reached number one on the "Billboard" Hot 100 on August 11, 1984, staying there for three weeks, and at number two on the UK Singles Chart on September 16, 1984, staying there for three weeks.', 'node_id': '7876f93d-8a46-40f0-bdc7-b653fadaba3a', 'score': 0.44967806339263916}, {'text': 'Ray Erskine Parker Jr. (born May 1, 1954) is an American guitarist, singer-songwriter,  record producer, and actor, best known for writing and performing the theme song to the movie "Ghostbusters", for his solo music, and for performing with his band, Raydio, and with Barry White.', 'node_id': '86a72dce-6faf-4d99-a87f-3b0c3e844b26', 'score': 0.5483460426330566}, {'text': 'The following is a list of "Saturday Night Live" cast members, past and present. The cast members of "Saturday Night Live" were originally referred to as the "Not Ready For Prime Time Players."', 'node_id': '9203c06e-1b7b-4087-8822-a8695a4a0f13', 'score': 1.1657357215881348}, {'text': 'The song is also a part of the "Rock Band" downloadable content catalog. The song was also featured in the "Project Gotham Racing 4". The musical video for the song was filmed in an abandoned hospital in which some scenes from the 1984 horror film "A Nightmare on Elm Street" were filmed. "Stricken" was used as official theme for WWE\'s PPV New Year\'s Revolution, in 2006.', 'node_id': '9cd90181-e616-4370-a2e7-37b998988f6a', 'score': 1.1905529499053955}, {'text': 'He wrote the theme music for MTV\'s "Road Rules", as well as producing music for many other TV shows such as "", "TMZ on TV", "America\'s Next Top Model", ABC\'s "Making The Band", "Extra", "Alias" and the Keanu Reeves film "The Watcher".', 'node_id': 'f7d649a3-be71-4b9c-8092-ab8c1e453135', 'score': 1.2208904027938843}], 'consistency_check': 'CONSISTENT', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'NEUTRAL', 'response': 'ENTAILMENT'}, 'latency': 1.601314201951027, 'vram_usage': 1.54052734375}
