 The differences between them relate to climate. They are as follows:", 'node_id': 'c4baa248-80dc-4154-bc27-c72b9a71234c', 'score': 0.9343469738960266}, {'text': 'North of the Arctic Circle, the sun is above the horizon for twenty-four continuous hours at least once per year (and therefore visible at midnight) and below the horizon for twenty-four continuous hours at least once per year (and therefore not visible at noon); this is also true within the equivalent polar circle in the Southern Hemisphere, the Antarctic Circle.', 'node_id': '3ecca4f4-1a22-42db-9fdc-4428101007e3', 'score': 1.0815649032592773}], 'consistency_check': 'MISSING', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'NEUTRAL', 'response': 'NEUTRAL'}, 'latency': 0.7649243380874395, 'vram_usage': 1.42333984375}
