e Insurance Company and later started his own insurance brokerage business in Columbus, Ohio. He was elected to the College Football Hall of Fame in 1989.', 'node_id': 'afaa6460-84bf-4901-8696-fa65cc51288d', 'score': 1.087568998336792}, {'text': "Thomas Wyatt Wilson Binford (April 6, 1924 – January 14, 1999) was an Indianapolis-based entrepreneur and philanthropist. One of Indianapolis' most influential men, Thomas W. Binford was a pioneer, visionary and civil rights leader. He participated in civic, philanthropic, cultural and political aspects of the city and state and was valued for his sensitivity, wise counsel, personal and financial support, and sincerity.", 'node_id': '17953d7a-a49a-4137-826c-7d2514aa7d7e', 'score': 1.1314727067947388}], 'consistency_check': 'CONSISTENT', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'CONTRADICTION', 'response': 'CONTRADICTION'}, 'latency': 0.760332316160202, 'vram_usage': 1.25927734375}
