 34%|███▍      | 171/500 [29:06<1:10:50, 12.92s/it]['Suffolk County'] {'response': 'The suburban county on Long Island and the easternmost county in the U.S. state of New York that is the location of the village called Lindenhurst is Suffolk County. Suffolk County is noted for being the fourth-most populous county in New York, with a population of 1,493,350 as of the 2010 census. The county seat is Riverhead, although most county offices are located in Hauppauge. Lindenhurst is situated on the southern shore of Long Island within this county.', 'query': 'What suburban county on Long Island and the easternmost county in the U.S. state of New York is the location of a village called Lindenhurst?', 'retrieved_context': [{'text': 'Lindenhurst is a village in Suffolk County, New York, United States, on the southern shore of Long Island in the town of Babylon. The population was 27,253 at the 2010 census.', 'node_id': '492cc8e0-11ba-4c3b-b748-f3c7efb4ffd6', 'score': 0.4457792639732361}, {'text': 'However, many people in the New York metropolitan area (even those living in Brooklyn and Queens) colloquially use the term "Long Island" (or "The Island") exclusively to refer to the Nassau–Suffolk county area collectively, which is mainly suburban in character. The majority of New York City residents now live on Long Island.', 'node_id': '21b2b7a6-dfaa-478c-934d-c29b5b4c4f1e', 'score': 0.6019827723503113}, {'text': 'The Long Island is a large, densely-populated island off the East Coast of the United States, beginning at New York Harbor just 0.35 miles (0.56\xa0km) from Manhattan Island and extending eastward into the Atlantic Ocean. The island comprises four counties in the U.S. state of New York: Kings and Queens (which comprise the New York City boroughs of Brooklyn and Queens, respectively) to the west; and Nassau and Suffolk to the east.', 'node_id': '9055b1da-e35d-4997-b0eb-94fae181d09b', 'score': 0.6314234733581543}, {'text': "Nassau County is a suburban county on the western side of Long Island in the U.S. state of New York. At the 2010 census, the county's population was 1,339,532, estimated to have increased to 1,361,500 in 2016. The county seat is in the Village of Garden City, within the boundaries of the Mineola 11501 zip code.", 'node_id': 'bb416e23-96c6-47f7-9d6c-405f375771fb', 'score': 0.6930062174797058}, {'text': "Suffolk County is a suburban county on Long Island and the easternmost county in the U.S. state of New York. As of the 2010 census, the county's population was 1,493,350, estimated to have decreased to 1,492,583 in 2016, making it the fourth-most populous county in New York. Its county seat is Riverhead, though most county offices are located in Hauppauge. The county was named after the county of Suffolk in England, from where its earliest European settlers came.", 'node_id': '479c8895-bb3e-44cf-8b75-18246273b692', 'score': 0.7691177129745483}], 'consistency_check': 'CONFLICT', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'CONTRADICTION', 'response': 'ENTAILMENT'}, 'latency': 1.553392231464386, 'vram_usage': 1.38818359375}
