['Steyr Mannlicher'] {'response': 'Steyr Mannlicher is based in Sankt Ulrich bei Steyr, Austria. It is a firearms manufacturer that was originally part of Steyr-Daimler-Puch. The company became independent when the conglomerate was broken up in 1989.', 'query': 'What is based in Sankt Ulrich bei Steyr, Austria? ', 'retrieved_context': [{'text': 'Sankt Ulrich bei Steyr is a municipality in the district of Steyr-Land in the Austrian state of Upper Austria.', 'node_id': '81ed8132-90f8-44be-b9b2-181dc99bcaa9', 'score': 21.024703979492188}, {'text': 'Steyr Mannlicher is a firearms manufacturer based in Sankt Ulrich bei Steyr, Austria. Originally part of Steyr-Daimler-Puch, it became independent when the conglomerate was broken up in 1989.', 'node_id': '06cad100-dadd-4eee-bd5b-3f9229b16211', 'score': 20.309953689575195}, {'text': 'Sankt Lorenzen bei Knittelfeld is a former municipality in the district of Murtal in Styria, Austria. Since the 2015 Styria municipal structural reform, it is part of the municipality Sankt Margarethen bei Knittelfeld.', 'node_id': '484eb335-2d08-409d-8f9f-6a981f125354', 'score': 12.217327117919922}, {'text': 'Sankt Ulrich im Mühlkreis is a municipality in the district of Rohrbach in the Austrian state of Upper Austria.', 'node_id': 'b417c4a4-6387-4776-a963-81f772479073', 'score': 11.045654296875}, {'text': 'Sankt Ulrich am Pillersee is a municipality in the Kitzbühel district, in midwestern Austria, and is located 16.4 km northeast of Kitzbühel as well as 11 km west of Sankt Johann in Tirol.', 'node_id': '422238d8-c8ad-424a-aba7-0852e95626ab', 'score': 10.56827449798584}, {'text': 'Saint Ulrich (German: "Sankt Ulrich, Sankt-Ulrich" ) or Saint Ulric may refer to four saints:', 'node_id': '4edf8dfd-95c3-4920-b16a-34b8c7d45388', 'score': 10.081070899963379}, {'text': 'Sankt Ulrich am Waasen is a former municipality in the district of Leibnitz in Styria, Austria. Since the 2015 Styria municipal structural reform, it is part of the municipality Heiligenkreuz am Waasen.', 'node_id': 'cf23e323-8025-43c1-949c-a146c3a3b451', 'score': 9.503087997436523}, {'text': 'St. Ulrich\'s and St. Afra\'s Abbey, Augsburg (German: "Kloster Sankt Ulrich und Afra Augsburg" ) is a former Benedictine abbey dedicated to Saint Ulrich and Saint Afra in the south of the old city in Augsburg, Bavaria.', 'node_id': 'f61633d5-fc10-4b12-ac1b-ec41710d5ed5', 'score': 7.9872002601623535}, {'text': 'Feldkirchen in Kärnten (Slovene: "Trg" ) is a town in the Austrian state of Carinthia and the capital of the district of the same name. It consists of the Katastralgemeinden "Fasching", "Feldkirchen", "Glanhofen", "Gradisch", "Hoefling", "Klein Sankt Veit", "Pernegg", "Rabensdorf", "Sankt Ulrich", "Sittich", "Tschwarzen" and "Waiern".', 'node_id': '0c7aac2f-5865-44ec-ab9e-141c8e3b3df7', 'score': 7.155117034912109}, {'text': 'The Steyr M1912, also known as the Steyr-Hahn, is a semi-automatic pistol developed in 1911 by the Austrian firm Steyr Mannlicher and designed by Karel Krnka, based on the mechanism of the Roth–Steyr M1907. It was developed for the Austro-Hungarian Army and adopted in 1912 as the M1912. It was in service in a limited capacity for the Wehrmacht until the end of World War II.', 'node_id': '8780c2c3-d404-4ed2-b846-ad5acf7216cb', 'score': 6.6715240478515625}], 'consistency_check': 'CONSISTENT', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'ENTAILMENT', 'response': 'ENTAILMENT'}, 'latency': 0.906791664659977, 'vram_usage': 0.0}
