 35%|███▍      | 173/500 [29:53<1:37:48, 17.95s/it]['US 60'] {'response': "U.S. Highway 60 gives access to Zilpo Road and is also known as the Midland Trail. The byway starts south of Morehead, Kentucky, and can be accessed by this highway, which is part of the historical auto trail era. The southern portion of the highway, along with modern SR 168, forms part of the Midland Trail, highlighting its significance in the region's transportation history.", 'query': 'What U.S Highway gives access to Zilpo Road, and is also known as Midland Trail?', 'retrieved_context': [{'text': 'Zilpo Road is a National Forest Scenic Byway in the forested hills of eastern Kentucky, United States. The nine mile byway starts south of Morehead, Kentucky and can be accessed by U.S. Highway 60. The byway travels through the Daniel Boone National Forest and ends on the western shore of Cave Run Lake at the Zilpo Recreation Area. It follows FSR 918, which is a two lane paved road suitable for all motor vehicles and is usually open throughout the year.', 'node_id': 'd5652588-5ad0-4780-8208-3fe66caaf380', 'score': 0.6595631241798401}, {'text': 'The southern portion of the highway, along with modern SR 168, dates to the auto trail era, forming part of the Midland Trail.', 'node_id': '5f1daf0d-3e10-4e09-9c59-fe0565b1f447', 'score': 0.8080723881721497}, {'text': 'Route 78) which becomes a divided freeway after State Route 175.', 'node_id': '5bf90ae8-65bd-4232-ac1d-f3ee13799266', 'score': 1.0261306762695312}, {'text': 'The Lakeview Drive (also known as North Shore Road and the Road to Nowhere) is a 6.5 mi road, split in two segments, located along the north shore of Fontana Lake, wholly within the Great Smoky Mountains National Park. The scenic road, which was never completed, features an unused road tunnel and connects to various hiking and horse riding trails in the area.', 'node_id': '9a898a19-9033-44b5-9a2d-8a74c1f0f27d', 'score': 1.0755831003189087}, {'text': 'Its southern terminus is at U.S. 441 on the boundary between Great Smoky Mountains National Park and the Cherokee Indian Reservation in North Carolina, from which it travels north to Shenandoah National Park in Virginia. The roadway continues through Shenandoah as Skyline Drive, a similar scenic road which is managed by a different National Park Service unit.', 'node_id': 'b4b2ce98-894d-41db-8dee-a2f6881071e3', 'score': 1.0887233018875122}], 'consistency_check': 'MISSING', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'CONTRADICTION', 'response': 'NEUTRAL'}, 'latency': 1.0444537457078695, 'vram_usage': 1.27099609375}
