['Rickenbacker International Airport'] {'response': 'The provided context is insufficient regarding the proximity of Luis Muñoz Marín International Airport to Cleveland, Ohio, compared to Rickenbacker International Airport. The context only provides information about the locations and characteristics of the two airports but does not specify their distances from Cleveland.', 'query': 'Which airport is closer to Cleaveland, Ohio, Luis Muñoz Marín International Airport or Rickenbacker International Airport?', 'retrieved_context': [{'text': 'Rickenbacker International is primarily a cargo airport for the city of Columbus, although since 2012 it has served an increasing number of passenger flights as well as charter carriers.', 'node_id': '2aac27c4-9ed1-4b25-a5b7-91a529789cb3', 'score': 0.7325242757797241}, {'text': 'Rickenbacker International Airport (IATA: LCK, ICAO: KLCK, FAA LID: LCK) is a civil-military public airport 10 mi south of downtown Columbus, near Lockbourne in southern Franklin County, Ohio, United States. The south end of the airport extends into Pickaway County. The base was named for flying ace and Columbus native Eddie Rickenbacker. It is managed by the Columbus Regional Airport Authority, which also operates John Glenn Columbus International Airport and Bolton Field.', 'node_id': '8a1214c9-cfa5-4107-9d49-3688989198ee', 'score': 0.7407860159873962}, {'text': 'Luis Muñoz Marín International Airport (IATA: SJU, ICAO: TJSJ, FAA LID: SJU) (Spanish: "Aeropuerto Internacional Luis Muñoz Marín" , Or Isla Verde International Airport/Aeropuerto Internacional de Isla Verde) is a joint civil-military international airport named for Puerto Rico\'s first democratically elected governor and located in suburban Carolina, Puerto Rico, 3 mi southeast of San Juan. It is the busiest airport in the Caribbean region by passenger traffic.', 'node_id': 'b790998c-88e5-4062-9933-7944fcf8ced3', 'score': 0.9118679761886597}, {'text': 'OR Tambo International Airport is in the Kempton Park area of Ekurhuleni.', 'node_id': 'da256490-8bfd-4df0-978c-fdae771004a3', 'score': 0.9613943696022034}, {'text': 'Aerostar Airport Holdings, LLC is the public–private partnership, privately held company, and limited liability company that operates and manages the Luis Muñoz Marín International Airport on behalf of the Puerto Rico Ports Authority. The company is an equitable joint venture between Highstar Capital, an infrastructure investment firm, and Grupo Aeroportuario del Sureste, a Mexican airport management firm. Aerostar has a forty-year lease to manage and upgrade the airport, including the investment of nearly $1.4 billion in capital improvements over the course of the lease.', 'node_id': '738f2366-6b05-4040-b27a-a80706f79329', 'score': 1.1269670724868774}], 'consistency_check': 'CONSISTENT', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'NEUTRAL', 'response': 'NEUTRAL'}, 'latency': 0.8789336699992418, 'vram_usage': 1.31787109375}
