 49%|████▉     | 247/500 [45:49<52:47, 12.52s/it]['ten weeks'] {'response': 'The provided context is insufficient regarding how many weeks the lead single from Culture Beat\'s second studio album spent at number one on the "RPM" Dance chart in Canada.', 'query': 'How many weeks did the lead single from Culture Beat\'s second studio album spend at number one on the "RPM" Dance chart in Canada?', 'retrieved_context': [{'text': 'It peaked at number 6 on the U.S. "Billboard" Hot Country Singles & Tracks chart and at number 7 on the Canadian "RPM" Country Tracks chart.', 'node_id': '15c3df41-651a-4679-ac3f-69ce9cc05ec0', 'score': 0.9482002854347229}, {'text': "In 2012, Shy FX made a 're-edit' of the song that was re-released to radio. This version reached number 22 on the UK Singles Chart and number 39 on the Irish Singles Chart. The sales of all versions are combined together enabling it to have sold in excess of 600,000 copies, receiving a Platinum certification, despite never reaching the top twenty of the UK Singles Chart.", 'node_id': '64266c06-3a1b-465a-9cf1-2924d4a6ebcf', 'score': 1.0660597085952759}, {'text': 'In the US, the track reached number 59 on the "Billboard" Hot 100 singles chart, becoming the band\'s second single to hit the chart after "There\'s No Other Way". It also reached number 4 on the Modern Rock songs chart.', 'node_id': '55c8d85b-6775-4842-bc23-72a252ffa8b7', 'score': 1.0693912506103516}, {'text': 'It peaked at number one on Finland\'s Official List and number 6 on the "Billboard" Dance/Electronic Albums chart in the United States. Darude\'s second studio album, "Rush", reached number 11 on the "Billboard" dance chart in 2003 and number 4 on weekly album chart in Finland.', 'node_id': '4308823a-442a-4645-a339-357b18a5511f', 'score': 1.0766048431396484}, {'text': 'In the latter country, the song peaked at number two on the "Billboard" Hot 100, where it remained for nine weeks during the summer of 1996, kept from number one by Los Del Rio\'s "Macarena". Despite this, the song was number one on the Hot 100 Airplay chart for thirteen weeks and the "Billboard" Top 40 Mainstream chart for eleven weeks, becoming one of the most played songs of the 1990s.', 'node_id': '34b55708-0447-45af-b844-243a7cb7fd45', 'score': 1.0816636085510254}], 'consistency_check': 'MISSING', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'CONTRADICTION', 'response': 'NEUTRAL'}, 'latency': 0.6960734948515892, 'vram_usage': 1.36474609375}
