['ten weeks'] {'response': 'The lead single from Culture Beat\'s second studio album, "Serenity," is "Mr. Vain." According to the provided context, "Mr. Vain" spent ten weeks at number one on the "RPM" Dance chart in Canada.', 'query': 'How many weeks did the lead single from Culture Beat\'s second studio album spend at number one on the "RPM" Dance chart in Canada?', 'retrieved_context': [{'text': '"Mr. Vain" is a song by German Eurodance group Culture Beat. It was released in April 1993 as the lead single from the album "Serenity". The song achieved huge success worldwide, reaching number one in Australia, Austria, Germany, Ireland, Italy, the Netherlands, Norway, Switzerland, and the United Kingdom. It also spent ten weeks at number one on the "RPM" Dance chart in Canada.', 'node_id': '9b690490-eb61-4df7-a523-b1dedba19857', 'score': 19.520917892456055}, {'text': '"No Deeper Meaning" is a song written by Jay Supreme and Nosie Katzmann, and recorded by the German eurodance band Culture Beat. It was released in June 1991 as the fourth and final single from their first studio album "Horizon". A CD maxi with new remixes was also available, but it was marketed at the same time as the other media. The song reached number 5 in the Netherlands and peaked at number 3 on the "RPM" Dance Chart in Canada.', 'node_id': '7c93712f-3637-4a8e-83d8-ccde268b18ad', 'score': 16.283771514892578}, {'text': 'It peaked at number one on Finland\'s Official List and number 6 on the "Billboard" Dance/Electronic Albums chart in the United States. Darude\'s second studio album, "Rush", reached number 11 on the "Billboard" dance chart in 2003 and number 4 on weekly album chart in Finland.', 'node_id': '4308823a-442a-4645-a339-357b18a5511f', 'score': 14.9819974899292}, {'text': '"Star Guitar" is the second single from The Chemical Brothers 2002 studio album "Come with Us". The song reached number eight in the UK Singles Chart, number two on the American dance chart and number one in the UK Dance Chart. The song was greeted with praise from critics.', 'node_id': '1c5c8a51-d1ec-4bad-bd8d-8cf2dc2cf85d', 'score': 14.478671073913574}, {'text': '"Stand and Deliver" is a song by English new wave band Adam and the Ants, released as the lead single from their third studio album, "Prince Charming" (1981). The song entered the UK Singles Chart at number one on 9 May 1981, and remained there for five weeks. It has sold 1.03 million copies in the UK. On the US Dance chart, "Stand and Deliver" peaked at #38, (along with the B side, "Beat My Guest").', 'node_id': '8ab7f72d-b6dd-48c2-aa1a-45547e98ae27', 'score': 14.437374114990234}, {'text': "Love in a Sleeper is the final studio album released by German euro-disco group Silver Convention, which at the time consisted of vocalists Ramona Wulf, Rhonda Heath and Zenda Jacks. The album managed to chart in the RPM 's disco album chart, peaking #11. The single Spend The Night With Me peaked #80 in the Billboard R&B Singles chart, #10 in Dance Music/Club Play Singles and #12 in Canadian Dance Chart.", 'node_id': 'b8fe4a86-8eb4-4f87-a547-d29c950affdd', 'score': 13.81968879699707}, {'text': '"Animal" is the lead single from Neon Trees\' debut studio album, "Habits". It debuted in June 2010 at number 100 on the "Billboard" Hot 100 and has reached a peak of number 13 in its twenty-two week on the chart. In Canada, the song debuted at number 95 on the Canadian Hot 100 and has climbed to number 29. The song has reached number one on the "Billboard" Alternative Songs chart after 32 weeks, making "Animal" their first number-one song on a "Billboard" chart.', 'node_id': '429eb27d-b4c9-4f31-8d69-58267280c575', 'score': 13.347733497619629}, {'text': '"Last Dance" is a song by English singer Dua Lipa from her eponymous debut studio album (2017). Lipa wrote the song with Stephen "Koz" Kozmeniuk and Talay Riley, with Kozmeniuk handling the song\'s production. It was released on 9 February 2016 as the album\'s second single. The track appears on the deluxe edition of "Dua Lipa". It peaked at number four on the "Billboard" Twitter Emerging Artists chart, spending seven weeks on it.', 'node_id': 'fc3d45c9-d695-4002-9842-2a4071019fa7', 'score': 12.863945007324219}, {'text': 'Serenity is the second studio album by German Eurodance band Culture Beat, released in 1993. It includes the single "Mr. Vain", which topped the charts across Europe and Australia.', 'node_id': 'd860cf3f-c321-49d7-a784-c2636c897b66', 'score': 12.610605239868164}, {'text': '"Tidal Wave" is the third single by British DJ and record producer Sub Focus to be released from his second studio album "Torus". The song features vocals from Alpines. The song peaked at number 12 on the UK Singles Chart and number 4 on the UK Dance Chart, making it his highest-charting single until "Endorphins" and "Turn Back Time", which both peaked at number 10 on the UK Singles Chart. It is still his highest-charting single on the UK Dance Chart and his biggest-selling single.', 'node_id': '3e88cb09-f6b5-4e22-ad3d-27e76faa025c', 'score': 12.158522605895996}], 'consistency_check': 'CONSISTENT', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'CONTRADICTION', 'response': 'ENTAILMENT'}, 'latency': 0.949168000370264, 'vram_usage': 0.0}
