 50%|█████     | 250/500 [46:18<42:07, 10.11s/it]['Memphis International Airport'] {'response': 'Memphis International Airport is located in Tennessee, specifically seven miles southeast of downtown Memphis in Shelby County. In contrast, Southwest Georgia Regional Airport is located in Georgia, three nautical miles southwest of the central business district of Albany in Dougherty County. Therefore, the airport situated in Tennessee between the two is Memphis International Airport.', 'query': 'In between Memphis International Airport and Southwest Georgia Regional Airport which one is in Tennessee?', 'retrieved_context': [{'text': 'Memphis International Airport (IATA: MEM, ICAO: KMEM, FAA LID: MEM) is a civil-military airport seven miles (11.2 km) southeast of downtown Memphis in Shelby County, Tennessee, United States.', 'node_id': 'a38890b7-38bf-483b-b721-ee9f1eabbf70', 'score': 0.5833255052566528}, {'text': 'Southwest Georgia Regional Airport (IATA: ABY, ICAO: KABY, FAA LID: ABY) is a city owned, public use airport located three nautical miles (6 km) southwest of the central business district of Albany, a city in Dougherty County, Georgia, United States. It is served by commercial passenger airlines.', 'node_id': '62cf55de-8acc-4c81-8f4b-2f59c2179f44', 'score': 0.7693184614181519}, {'text': 'West Georgia Regional Airport (ICAO: KCTJ,\xa0FAA LID: CTJ) , also known as O. V. Gray Field, is a public use airport located five nautical miles (9 km) northwest of the central business district of Carrollton, in Carroll County, Georgia, United States. It is owned by the West Georgia Airport Authority.', 'node_id': '7451f4b5-8a17-493b-9e73-30370737a31a', 'score': 0.8710507750511169}, {'text': "It is near interstate highways I-65, I-69, I-70 and I-74, all of which connect to the city's I-465 beltway. The passenger terminal was the first designed and built in the United States after the September 11, 2001 attacks. The airport is also home to a FedEx Express hub, the company's second-largest after the SuperHub at Memphis International Airport. Opened in 1988, the hub has been expanded three times.", 'node_id': 'bce01f0e-2fca-40ec-9190-30a42be7a4d2', 'score': 0.9147643446922302}, {'text': 'Alexander Kartveli Batumi International Airport (IATA: BUS,\xa0ICAO: UGSB) is an airport located 2 km south of Batumi, a city on the Black Sea coast and capital of Adjara, an autonomous republic in southwest Georgia. The airport is 20 km northeast of Hopa, Turkey, and serves as a domestic and international airport for Georgia and northeastern Turkey.', 'node_id': '015f5630-a897-4441-8ece-ab250971de76', 'score': 0.9312151670455933}], 'consistency_check': 'MISSING', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'NEUTRAL', 'response': 'ENTAILMENT'}, 'latency': 0.7528617270290852, 'vram_usage': 1.21240234375}
