 58%|█████▊    | 289/500 [52:43<43:07, 12.26s/it]['The Raconteurs'] {'response': 'The provided context is insufficient regarding the number of members in each band. However, based on general knowledge, Muse consists of three members: Matt Bellamy, Chris Wolstenholme, and Dominic Howard. The Raconteurs, on the other hand, consists of four members: Jack White, Brendan Benson, Jack Lawrence, and Patrick Keeler. Therefore, The Raconteurs has more members than Muse.', 'query': 'Which band has more members, Muse or The Raconteurs?', 'retrieved_context': [{'text': 'Muse are an English rock band from Teignmouth, Devon, formed in 1994. The band consists of Matt Bellamy (lead vocals, guitar, piano, keyboards), Chris Wolstenholme (bass guitar, backing vocals, keyboards) and Dominic Howard (drums, percussion).', 'node_id': 'cc15c973-31ab-4869-ac8a-cd8fbec82e0b', 'score': 0.680266261100769}, {'text': 'The band has toured with many bands including MewithoutYou, Silverstein, Bayside, Further Seems Forever, Zao, Embodyment, Shelter, and Tantrum of the Muse, Few Left Standing, and Underoath.', 'node_id': '943c5d64-226f-4160-a3a0-4aebcd1d16d1', 'score': 0.7943922281265259}, {'text': 'The Raconteurs , also known as The Saboteurs in Australia, is an American rock supergroup that was formed in Detroit, Michigan, featuring four musicians associated with earlier musical projects: Jack White (formerly of The White Stripes, currently The Dead Weather, as well as solo), Brendan Benson (solo), Jack Lawrence (of The Greenhornes, Blanche and The Dead Weather), and Patrick Keeler (also of The Greenhornes).', 'node_id': '7672f97e-e89d-4420-af0a-c773e92cd571', 'score': 0.8841147422790527}, {'text': 'Tantrum of the Muse was a heavy metal art rock band based out of Lancaster County, Pennsylvania. The band formed in 1998 and disbanded in 2004. The band members refers to their existence as "The Tantrum Reign of Terror".', 'node_id': 'd2d29154-8a4e-49a3-8c1b-4af75e744b55', 'score': 1.0444252490997314}, {'text': "A Seaside Rendezvous was a 2009 duo of concerts by English alternative rock band Muse. Held at The Den in Teignmouth, Devon, the town in which the band's members spent their childhoods and began their musical careers, the homecoming concerts were the band's first shows in the town for 15 years. It is believed that the name 'Seaside Rendezvous' was taken from the Queen song of the same name (Queen being a major influence on the band).", 'node_id': '9d6efd05-953d-4c09-818c-fe17c1ab5ea8', 'score': 1.0610851049423218}], 'consistency_check': 'MISSING', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'NEUTRAL', 'response': 'ENTAILMENT'}, 'latency': 1.2795763835310936, 'vram_usage': 1.18896484375}
