 62%|██████▏   | 308/500 [56:33<33:32, 10.48s/it]["Arthur's Magazine"] {'response': "Arthur's Magazine was started first. It was published in Philadelphia from 1844 to 1846, while First for Women was started later in 1989. Therefore, Arthur's Magazine predates First for Women by 145 years.", 'query': "Which magazine was started first Arthur's Magazine or First for Women?", 'retrieved_context': [{'text': 'Arthur\'s Magazine (1844–1846) was an American literary periodical published in Philadelphia in the 19th century. Edited by T.S. Arthur, it featured work by Edgar A. Poe, J.H. Ingraham, Sarah Josepha Hale, Thomas G. Spear, and others. In May 1846 it was merged into "Godey\'s Lady\'s Book".', 'node_id': 'edccdb69-888d-4a34-8490-5d4fc2e1a6a0', 'score': 0.5408766865730286}, {'text': "First for Women is a woman's magazine published by Bauer Media Group in the USA. The magazine was started in 1989. It is based in Englewood Cliffs, New Jersey. In 2011 the circulation of the magazine was 1,310,696 copies.", 'node_id': '70a45dff-5572-44d5-ba23-0de25c631aa3', 'score': 0.6585443615913391}, {'text': 'In 1898 the first women\'s magazine was published in China. The number of women\'s magazines has increased in the country since the late 1980s. In addition to national titles international magazines are also published in the country. "Madame Figaro", and "Elle" are among such titles both of which entered into the Chinese market in 1988. In 1998 "Cosmopolitan" began to be published in the country. "Esquire" is the first international men\'s magazine which entered into the magazine market in China in 1999.', 'node_id': '8abd81e7-a62a-4b53-bc67-7467f7cd1ee9', 'score': 0.787218451499939}, {'text': 'The first women\'s magazine was published in Malaysia in 1932. In the 2000s there were nearly fifty local titles addressing women in the country. These magazines also include those having an Islamic perspective. Some international women\'s magazines are also published in Malaysia. One of them is "Elle Malaysia", which was first published in March 2014. Another one, "Women’s Health", was started in April 2015. Comic magazines and film magazines are also common in Malaysia.', 'node_id': '99d80a15-df4d-4486-b530-b84d289150a4', 'score': 0.8961646556854248}, {'text': "Rabotnitsa (Russian: Работница ; English: The Woman Worker ) is a women's journal, published in the Soviet Union and Russia and one of the oldest Russian magazines for women and families. Founded in 1914, and first published on Women's Day, it is the first socialist women's journal, and the most politically left of the women's periodicals. While the journal's beginnings are attributed to Lenin and several women who were close to him, he did not contribute to the first seven issues.", 'node_id': '39924ffa-e78e-400b-9396-e36c25b19fe8', 'score': 1.030657410621643}], 'consistency_check': 'MISSING', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'NEUTRAL', 'response': 'ENTAILMENT'}, 'latency': 0.8151999078691006, 'vram_usage': 1.18896484375}
