e': 1.1747387647628784}, {'text': 'Radharc was an Irish television documentary series broadcast by RTÉ Television from 1962 until 1996. The documentaries were created by a film unit funded by the Catholic Archbishop of Dublin, John Charles McQuaid, in anticipation of the inauguration of television broadcasting in Ireland by RTÉ in December 1961. The film unit was staffed exclusively by Catholic priests, including Joe Dunn, Desmond Forristal, and Peter Lemass. The Irish language word "radharc" means vision, view, or panorama.', 'node_id': '6594b4cb-c168-4855-adb3-e779f098a0cd', 'score': 1.18569016456604}, {'text': 'Frances "Franny" Healy (born 24 August 1970) is an Irish actress, comedian, radio personality and TV presenter. She starred as "Niamh Corrigan" in the famous BBC Scotland soap opera "River City". Other television credits include Taggart and the Irish soap Fair City. Film credits include The Magdalene Sisters and The Serpent\'s Kiss, where she starred alongside Ewan McGregor. Theatre credits include "The Vagina Monologues", "The Seagull" and "Juno and the Paycock".', 'node_id': 'd99e16f6-ef44-4808-890a-138da4cbae61', 'score': 1.1917874813079834}], 'consistency_check': 'MISSING', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'CONTRADICTION', 'response': 'NEUTRAL'}, 'latency': 1.1867272425442934, 'vram_usage': 1.44677734375}
