 73%|███████▎  | 364/500 [1:04:46<25:12, 11.12s/it]['American'] {'response': 'The provided context is insufficient regarding the nationality of the male lead of the film Fishtales.', 'query': 'What nationality is the male lead of the film Fishtales?', 'retrieved_context': [{'text': 'Fishtales is a 2007 family comedy film directed by Alki David, and starring Billy Zane and Kelly Brook about a widowed father who falls in love with a mermaid. The film was released theatrically in the UK on 24 August 2007.', 'node_id': '0d8fb7a5-bb32-4ba9-bced-ccc78594f01a', 'score': 0.6258275508880615}, {'text': 'Manfish is a 1956 adventure film, released by United Artists in 1956 and originally filmed in DeLuxe Color. Filmed in Jamaica, it was released in Great Britain as "Calypso". It was based on the stories "The Gold-Bug" and "The Tell-Tale Heart" by Edgar Allan Poe. Actor John Bromfield starred as Captain Brannigan and Lon Chaney Jr. played the role of Swede. The leading female star was Tessa Prendergast, who played Alita.', 'node_id': '022128e6-fd0e-4d54-bca3-9a37843e82f4', 'score': 0.7113378047943115}, {'text': 'Detective Phil Fish is a fictional NYPD detective in the TV series "Barney Miller" and later in the spin off series "Fish". He was played by Abe Vigoda.', 'node_id': 'e5f86555-4385-472d-86ca-947918df479e', 'score': 1.021365761756897}, {'text': "The series' premise originated with Paul Attanasio, while David Shore, who is credited as creator, was primarily responsible for the conception of the title character. The series' executive producers included Shore, Attanasio, Attanasio's business partner Katie Jacobs, and film director Bryan Singer. It was filmed largely in Century City.", 'node_id': '40b53464-33d5-473c-90b2-73b79c7be2bc', 'score': 1.112527847290039}, {'text': 'The screenplay and lyrics, written by Hisashi Inōe and Morihisa Yamamoto, is based on the European literary fairy tale of the same name by Charles Perrault, expanded with elements of Alexandre Dumas-esque swashbuckling adventure and funny animal slapstick, with many other anthropomorphic animals ("kemono" in Japanese) in addition to the title character. The Tōei version of the character himself is named Pero, after Perrault.', 'node_id': '47f8f36e-6cf6-4acc-8f3d-b710abe4b7df', 'score': 1.114664912223816}], 'consistency_check': 'CONFLICT', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'CONTRADICTION', 'response': 'ENTAILMENT'}, 'latency': 0.5848038028925657, 'vram_usage': 1.17724609375}
