uitar, vocals) and Mark Rohan (drums) along with Don Hayes (lead guitar) and Dean Ball (bass guitar). After discovering that another band already existed in Louisville, Kentucky with the name "Blue Collar Band", the band added "Kentucky" to its name and thus became the Kentucky Blue Collar Band.', 'node_id': 'd861514f-53c0-4803-bb7f-f9d5bc587171', 'score': 0.9534505605697632}, {'text': 'They have released three studio albums which all achieved success. The band stopped performing in 2014.', 'node_id': 'a887c176-bdd0-4195-b38d-300d5297751e', 'score': 0.9563671350479126}], 'consistency_check': 'MISSING', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'NEUTRAL', 'response': 'ENTAILMENT'}, 'latency': 0.6159318741410971, 'vram_usage': 1.17724609375}
