['David Lee Roth'] {'response': "The provided context is insufficient regarding Cia Berg. However, it does state that David Lee Roth was inducted into the Rock and Roll Hall of Fame in 2007. Therefore, David Lee Roth was inducted into the Rock and Roll Hall of Fame, while there is no information provided about Cia Berg's induction status.", 'query': 'Who was inducted into the Rock and Roll Hall of Fame, David Lee Roth or Cia Berg?', 'retrieved_context': [{'text': 'David Lee Roth (born October 10, 1954) is an American rock vocalist, musician, songwriter, actor, author, and former radio personality. In 2007, he was inducted into the Rock and Roll Hall of Fame.', 'node_id': '014e38f6-5c61-4053-9743-a80299a94506', 'score': 0.40217703580856323}, {'text': 'The David Lee Roth Band was an American rock and roll band, formed in Pasadena, California in 1985 by Van Halen frontman David Lee Roth. Originally featuring a supergroup line-up of guitarist Steve Vai, bassist Billy Sheehan, and drummer Gregg Bissonette, the band released numerous popular songs and albums from the mid-1980s until the late 1990s.', 'node_id': '43ceb85c-b555-4942-93a9-a1e90b68e876', 'score': 0.8808533549308777}, {'text': 'He is the second youngest person (after Neil Peart) to be inducted into the "Modern Drummer\'s" "Hall of Fame", at 37 years of age.', 'node_id': '5ffff348-0140-4108-b507-cf050ddf009f', 'score': 1.0246548652648926}, {'text': 'David Lee Roth is an American rock music singer. His discography consists of six studio albums, one extended play, one compilation album, and twenty singles. Of his eight albums, four have been certified Gold or higher by the Recording Industry Association of America. "Eat \'Em and Smile", "Skyscraper" and "Crazy from the Heat" are certified Platinum, and "A Little Ain\'t Enough" is certified Gold. As of 2012, all of David Lee Roth\'s Warner Brothers LPs are due for recertification.', 'node_id': 'f3fb2ec2-7abe-4460-97e4-895dacaae33b', 'score': 1.0513134002685547}, {'text': 'Notably different from Howard Stern\'s program, or corporate "morning zoo" and "shock jock" formats which dominated morning radio at the time, Roth\'s show sounded similar to pirate radio, featuring ethnic and non-commercial rock music integrated with personal stories, occasionally uncomfortable debates on intellectual matters, and interviews with people Roth admired, such as guitarist Brian May, baseball player Johnny Damon, and Roth\'s uncle, Manny Roth.', 'node_id': 'e16ae22e-be93-4f6d-8930-313971cdba35', 'score': 1.0686602592468262}, {'text': 'Other well-known musicians in the David Lee Roth Band have include guitarist Jason Becker, guitarist Steve Hunter, guitarist John 5 (guitarist), bassist Matt Bissonette drummer Ray Luzier, and keyboardist Brett Tuggle. The band\'s well-known songs include "Yankee Rose", "Goin\' Crazy!", "Shy Boy", "Just Like Paradise", "Stand Up", "Damn Good", "A Little Ain\'t Enough", "She\'s My Machine", and "Slam Dunk!"', 'node_id': '0a810f56-4aae-444a-8104-78529d063973', 'score': 1.0911372900009155}, {'text': 'Their Top 10 R&B hits included "Work with Me, Annie", "It\'s Love Baby (24 Hours a Day)", "Annie Had a Baby", "The Hoochi Coochi Coo", "Teardrops on Your Letter", "Get It", "The Float" and "Nothing but Good". They received the Rhythm and Blues Foundation\'s prestigious Pioneer Award in 1992 and were inducted into the Vocal Group Hall of Fame in 1999. The group\'s lead singer, Hank Ballard, was inducted into the Rock and Roll Hall of Fame in 1990.', 'node_id': '255c8107-118d-48f1-aab8-7c66cc366240', 'score': 1.1050986051559448}, {'text': 'He was inducted into the Rock and Roll Hall of Fame as a member of Journey on April 7, 2017.', 'node_id': '3edc3a95-389d-427d-8ac5-5ee76a8dab67', 'score': 1.1120046377182007}, {'text': 'The Midnighters as a "group" were inducted into the Rock and Roll Hall of Fame on April 14, 2012.', 'node_id': '5546feae-bf5b-4335-a6f3-05b2c832ff37', 'score': 1.128369927406311}, {'text': 'He was inducted in the College Football Hall of Fame in 2006. An avid tennis player, Ward also displayed his skills at the Arthur Ashe Tennis Tournament in 1994.', 'node_id': 'aec6d5ab-98c3-419a-8b9f-8523223ed520', 'score': 1.1332917213439941}], 'consistency_check': 'CONSISTENT', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'CONTRADICTION', 'response': 'ENTAILMENT'}, 'latency': 3.945035630837083, 'vram_usage': 1.24755859375}
