 80%|████████  | 401/500 [1:09:59<15:57,  9.67s/it]['1952'] {'response': 'The provided context is insufficient regarding the year in which the halfback Billy Vessels won the Heisman Trophy.', 'query': "The Colts' first ever draft pick was a halfback who won the Heisman Trophy in what year?", 'retrieved_context': [{'text': 'This is a list of NFL Draft selections by the Indianapolis Colts. The first draft that the current incarnation of the Colts franchise participated in was 1953, in which they made halfback Billy Vessels of Oklahoma their first ever selection.', 'node_id': '1fea1476-a925-4f03-a18d-72393b7a687b', 'score': 0.5798858404159546}, {'text': "However, the Vols' defense could not stop Nebraska's rushing attack, giving up more than 400 yards on the ground in a 42–17 loss. As a senior, Manning won numerous awards. He was a consensus first-team All-American and won the Maxwell Award, the Davey O'Brien Award, the Johnny Unitas Award, and the Best College Football Player ESPY Award, among others. However, he did not win the Heisman Trophy, finishing runner-up to Charles Woodson, a CB from Michigan, and the only defensive player ever to win the Heisman Trophy.", 'node_id': 'ba819f0b-9e74-4f13-8367-ec45ce6ae956', 'score': 1.0108031034469604}, {'text': 'The 1997 Tennessee Volunteers football team represented the University of Tennessee during the 1997 NCAA Division I-A football season. Quarterback Peyton Manning had already completed his degree in three years, and had been projected to be the top overall pick in the 1997 NFL Draft, but returned to Tennessee for his senior year. The Volunteers opened the season with victories against Texas Tech and UCLA, but for the third time in his career, Manning fell to Florida, 33–20.', 'node_id': '1c3e27a8-e453-4572-a7a8-098b4d8230a1', 'score': 1.0141806602478027}, {'text': 'He also played in the East-West Shrine Game and was named MVP of the Senior Bowl. After the Senior Bowl he was drafted by Don Shula and The Miami Dolphins, his second year in the NFL he played both ways in a pre-season game and Coach Shula knew he had a guy that could back up every position on the offensive and defensive line as well as long snap. He earned a starting position at right guard and played against [[William Perry (American football)|the Fridge]] when the Dolphins beat the Chicago Bears on Monday Night Football to help keep the undefeated Dolphin record intact.', 'node_id': 'd578b83e-4e8b-4c95-9709-72973673d086', 'score': 1.0156327486038208}, {'text': "In 2015, Derrick Henry became the university's second Heisman winner.", 'node_id': '1f04b108-59f6-4880-9988-d166eff98fe0', 'score': 1.0370450019836426}], 'consistency_check': 'CONFLICT', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'CONTRADICTION', 'response': 'CONTRADICTION'}, 'latency': 0.8534576781094074, 'vram_usage': 1.27099609375}
