 84%|████████▎ | 418/500 [1:12:24<19:59, 14.63s/it]['Roy Orbison'] {'response': 'The American singer-songwriter known as "the Caruso of Rock" is Roy Kelton Orbison. He recorded on the Monument Records label and had hits such as "Pretty One" and "Uptown." Orbison is recognized for his distinctive, impassioned voice and complex song structures, which contributed to his acclaim in the music industry. His work during the early 1960s, particularly with Monument Records, solidified his status as a significant figure in rock music.', 'query': 'Which American singer-songwriter known as "the Caruso of Rock", recorded on the Monument Records label and had hits such as "Pretty One," and "Uptown"?', 'retrieved_context': [{'text': 'Roy Kelton Orbison (April 23, 1936 – December 6, 1988) was an American singer-songwriter known for his distinctive, impassioned voice, complex song structures, and dark emotional ballads. The combination led many critics to describe his music as operatic, nicknaming him "the Caruso of Rock" and "the Big O."', 'node_id': '198b64fa-01b2-490b-8c8a-46cf9b0aeb5c', 'score': 0.899286150932312}, {'text': 'Early Orbison is an album recorded by Roy Orbison on the Monument Records label at their studios in Hendersonville, Tennessee and released in 1964. Essentially a compilation of songs from his first two Monument albums, it is most noteworthy for containing "Pretty One", the "B" side of Orbison\'s second Monument single, "Uptown". Many Orbison fans believe "Pretty One" would have been his first major hit had it been promoted as an "A" side.', 'node_id': '2b73dd88-a2b4-473b-a724-83935fef03ed', 'score': 0.9530156850814819}, {'text': 'Thomas Edward Yorke (born 7 October 1968) is an English musician and composer best known as the singer and principal songwriter of the alternative rock band Radiohead. A multi-instrumentalist, Yorke mainly plays guitar and piano and works extensively with synthesisers, sequencers and programming. He is known for his falsetto vocals; in 2008, "Rolling Stone" ranked him the 66th greatest singer of all time.', 'node_id': 'd2cc500f-e4f8-4b23-ac07-ef16f3ae2713', 'score': 0.9975188970565796}, {'text': "This is believed to be Thom Yorke's first ever released recording, on which he played lead guitar and sang backing vocals; Yorke later became famous as the singer of Radiohead.", 'node_id': 'a1e58e81-d9bb-4b5e-8911-bba32e0b2db8', 'score': 1.0041213035583496}, {'text': '"Committed to Parkview", a Cash original, would be re-recorded in 1985 by Cash, Waylon Jennings, Kris Kristofferson and Willie Nelson, collectively known as The Highwaymen, on their first album, "Highwayman"; it is one of the few country songs sung from the perspective of a patient at a mental hospital.', 'node_id': '7756fe3c-373c-4d10-982d-f7e3b2c48a1d', 'score': 1.0230793952941895}], 'consistency_check': 'MISSING', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'CONTRADICTION', 'response': 'NEUTRAL'}, 'latency': 1.0612606350332499, 'vram_usage': 1.44677734375}
