['Showbox'] {'response': 'Lee Il-hyung\'s first feature film, "A Violent Prosecutor," was released in South Korea on February 3, 2016, by Showbox. This film marked his directorial debut and featured a notable cast including Hwang Jung-min, Kang Dong-won, Lee Sung-min, and Park Sung-woong. Showbox is known for distributing various films in South Korea, and "A Violent Prosecutor" was one of the significant releases under their banner.', 'query': "Lee Il-hyung's first feature film was released by which company ?", 'retrieved_context': [{'text': 'Lee Il-hyung is a South Korean film director and screenwriter. Prior to directing his first feature film "A Violent Prosecutor" (2016), Lee is an assistant director on films, such as "The Moonlight of Seoul" (2008), "My Way" (2011) and "" (2014), and commercial films.', 'node_id': '7758f281-220a-4c64-8254-d421a1952c27', 'score': 0.5664564371109009}, {'text': 'Lee Cheol-ha is a South Korean film director known for his stylish portraits of the human experience.', 'node_id': 'a23bbe75-1c6e-4ac7-ba83-bdee494acab7', 'score': 0.9173775315284729}, {'text': 'Chang Mi-hee (born December 8, 1958) is a South Korean actress active since 1976. She was born Lee Yun-hui in Seoul, South Korea in 1957. Chang debuted as an actress in 1976 as starring in "Seong Chun-hyang jeon" directed by Park Tae-won and TBC TV drama, "Haenyeo Dang-sil" (Sea Woman Dang-sil).', 'node_id': '2920b9fc-1f95-47c4-aeb1-419f75309b8a', 'score': 0.9718871116638184}, {'text': 'In 2010, he was named the "New Generation Producer" at the 18th Korean Culture Entertainment Awards, and in 2011 he was named as one of the most influential figures in the South Korean music industry by OSEN. Lee has recently started his own label, AB Entertainment, in which he has debuted his own girl group named EXID.', 'node_id': '0194bbb3-ea48-4514-95d3-03fcb3b2ec7f', 'score': 1.0352797508239746}, {'text': 'Seoul Station (Korean: 서울역 ) is a South Korean animated zombie drama film written and directed by Yeon Sang-ho. Released on August 18, 2016, the film stars Ryu Seung-ryong, Shim Eun-kyung and Lee Joon in the lead roles. The film was shown at the 2016 Edinburgh International Film Festival.', 'node_id': 'c064ff5c-fc16-4516-8270-a382a3cb044e', 'score': 1.0512504577636719}, {'text': 'Saigon Love Story is Vietnam\'s first movie musical filmed entirely on location in Vietnam including Saigon and Phan Thiet. One of the first films independently produced outside of the Communist controlled film industry, overseas Vietnamese director Ringo Le decided to return to his birthplace to shoot his first feature film project. "Saigon Love Story" had a highly acclaimed sold out screening at VC FilmFest 2006.', 'node_id': '72466928-80ba-41cc-aa28-73d9374b108b', 'score': 1.070847988128662}, {'text': 'Jo Hyun-jae (born May 9, 1980) is a South Korean actor. Jo made his entertainment debut as a singer in the four-member boy band Guardian, which disbanded after releasing their self-titled album in 1998. In 2000, after he drew popularity when he appeared in a commercial for sports drink Pocari Sweat, Jo began acting. He is best known for his leading roles in "Love Letter" (2003), "Only You" (2005), "Ballad of Seodong" (2005), and "49 Days" (2011).', 'node_id': '412e2608-ad13-40b5-af3b-4431038678a8', 'score': 1.0776116847991943}, {'text': 'She also acted in several dramas with supporting roles in "Ad Genius Lee Tae-baek", "God\'s Gift - 14 Days", and "Marriage, Not Dating". In 2014 she finally starred as a lead actress on MBC\'s weekend drama "Rosy Lovers" as Baek Jang Mi co-starring with actor Lee Jang Woo. CNN International Seoul listed Sunhwa as one of the nine rising "It" stars in Korean entertainment citing her as a "multi-tasking" artist.', 'node_id': 'fa1f7b5e-6041-4a7b-b6b0-6de7eed9da5c', 'score': 1.0971262454986572}, {'text': 'Lee Ji-eun (Korean: 이지은 ; born May 16, 1993), better known by her stage name IU (Korean: 아이유 ), is a South Korean singer, songwriter and actress. While still in middle school, IU auditioned for various talent agencies with ambitions of becoming a singer. She signed with LOEN Entertainment in 2007 as a trainee and began her music career at the age of 15 with her debut album, "Lost and Found".', 'node_id': '188e57b6-72f3-46c1-bcf8-23b42f430382', 'score': 1.1041321754455566}, {'text': 'Chae Jung-An (born Jang Jung-An on September 9, 1977) is a South Korean actress and singer.', 'node_id': 'aefeceba-dd7c-4658-8ce4-2bc6e1b6aa25', 'score': 1.1202497482299805}, {'text': 'Story of Wine (스토리 오브 와인 "Seutori obeu wain") is a 2008 South Korean film directed by Lee Cheol-ha and starring Lee Ki-woo. It is Korea\'s first interactive movie.', 'node_id': '037f2fb1-52b8-4d2b-a8ad-c161c83118a6', 'score': 1.1599667072296143}, {'text': 'Chang Dae-hwan (also Chang Dae-whan; born 21 March 1952) is a South Korean businessman. He is best known as the president of the "Maeil Business Newspaper", South Korea\'s main business daily. He also served a brief stint as South Korea\'s acting prime minister in August 2002 under president Kim Dae-jung, but the National Assembly voted not to confirm him.', 'node_id': 'bd530a14-995c-4a18-bc49-47b5e067fea4', 'score': 1.16053307056427}, {'text': "Han Myeong-sook (born March 24, 1944; Korean: 한명숙 ] ) was the Prime Minister of South Korea from April 2006 to March 2007. She is South Korea's first female prime minister (second female prime minister overall if the acting premiership of Chang Sang is included). She was from the United New Democratic Party (UNDP) as a member of the Korean National Assembly (representative) for Ilsan-gab, and is a graduate of Ewha Womans University in Seoul with a degree in French literature.", 'node_id': '73812bbd-4014-43f3-8ffa-267acca92ab2', 'score': 1.170732021331787}, {'text': 'The film was an official selection into the Panorama selection at the Shanghai International Film Festival 2006 and was nominated for the "Winds of Asia-Best New Film Award" at the Tokyo International Film Festival 2006. Currently, the film has been traveling throughout the United States in sold-out roadshow tours to help bring attention to Vietnamese films and artists. It was released on Valentine\'s Day in 2008 across Vietnam.', 'node_id': '68fd7901-aaf9-4f48-991b-72358ca7a787', 'score': 1.1717982292175293}, {'text': 'A Violent Prosecutor is a 2016 South Korean crime film directed by Lee Il-hyung, produced by Guk Su Ran and starring Hwang Jung-min, Kang Dong-won, Lee Sung-min and Park Sung-woong. It was released in South Korea on February 3, 2016 by Showbox.', 'node_id': 'c18bd071-d6b5-4180-835e-f06925aafd03', 'score': 1.1758337020874023}, {'text': 'He ventured into Tamil cinema in 1996 with the blockbuster, "Indian", which was India\'s Official Entry for the Best Foreign Language Film for the Academy Awards. He then produced films like "Kushi", "Run", "Boys", "Enakku 20 Unakku 18", "Dhool", "Ghilli", "7G Rainbow Colony","Arrambam", Bangaram, "Yennai Arindhaal" and "Vedalam".', 'node_id': 'bd54369e-87a4-4a05-91fd-2d349f4df63c', 'score': 1.179473638534546}, {'text': 'Lee Ho-yang (Korean: 이호양 ), better known by his stage name Shinsadong Tiger (Korean: 신사동호랭이 "Shinsadong Horaengi") is a South Korean music producer and songwriter. Even after debuting in 2001 at the age of 18 (19 in Korean age), he has worked many odd jobs to fund his music career. He has become a prominent figure in the Korean pop music industry and is responsible for a number of popular songs.', 'node_id': '565f0810-3a85-43cd-a99a-0ec0aa8dda3f', 'score': 1.1797561645507812}, {'text': 'Lee Hong-gi (; ] ; Japanese:イ•ホンギ) is a South Korean singer-songwriter, actor, writer, and fashion designer. He is best known for his singing abilities and being the main singer of the South Korean rock band F.T. Island. Lee released his first solo extended play "FM302" in South Korea on 18 November 2015 and his Japanese album "AM302" on 9 December 2015.', 'node_id': 'f0ca0538-6a93-49bd-a1e8-10c491dce699', 'score': 1.187560796737671}, {'text': 'The film is heavily influenced by the Korean movie "My Sassy Girl" and the English-language movie "You\'ve Got Mail".', 'node_id': '751a1f1a-a484-4df4-af8c-a3392bce3468', 'score': 1.1916364431381226}, {'text': 'Kwon So-hyun (born August 30, 1994), is a South Korean singer and actress. She was known as a member of the South Korean girl group 4Minute, under Cube Entertainment. She is also a former member of the South Korean girl group, Orange. Before June 15, 2016 (end of her contract with Cube), Sohyun left 4Minute and the record label along with members Nam Ji-hyun, Heo Ga-yoon, and Jeon Ji-yoon.', 'node_id': '68b90404-4a0c-47af-bcba-0108b1ceafc9', 'score': 1.211441159248352}], 'consistency_check': 'MISSING', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'CONTRADICTION', 'response': 'NEUTRAL'}, 'latency': 5.556022748351097, 'vram_usage': 1.21240234375}
