['United States'] {'response': 'The American Aircraft Penetrator was modified from the Bell UH-1B Iroquois, which is a helicopter produced by the United States military. The Bell UH-1 Iroquois, commonly known as "Huey," was developed by Bell Helicopter to meet a United States Army requirement for a medical evacuation and utility helicopter. Therefore, the nation responsible for the original helicopter is the United States.', 'query': "The American Aircraft Penetrator was modified from a helicopter produced by what nation's military?", 'retrieved_context': [{'text': 'The American Aircraft Penetrator, now referred as the Aerocraft Stealth Star 204 SS, was a gunship helicopter modified from the Bell UH-1B Iroquois with tandem seating for the pilots and a troop-carrying compartment.', 'node_id': '3456d967-7b64-40c2-adf8-ebca5df62d28', 'score': 14.176528930664062}, {'text': 'The American Aircraft International Penetrator was a military helicopter prototype conceived in 1990 as a gunship conversion of the Bell UH-1 Iroquois, aimed at ground insertion, close support and counter-insurgency roles.', 'node_id': '0f2153a1-171d-44c1-a828-b9885d5cdcf9', 'score': 12.822222709655762}, {'text': 'The Agusta AB.102 was an Italian helicopter produced in small numbers in the early 1960s. The aircraft was based on the mechanical components of a Bell 48 that Agusta incorporated into an all-new, streamlined fuselage. The first flight was on 3 February 1959 and the prototype was exhibited at that year\'s Paris Air Show in "faux" military colours. Only two production examples were built, operated by Elivie in a regular air service between Turin and Milan from 1961. However, the advent of turbine-powered helicopters in the 1960s soon rendered the AB.102 obsolete.', 'node_id': 'fe7625e1-2206-4b8e-8902-4f69e04628a0', 'score': 7.651676177978516}, {'text': 'The Harbin Z-20 or Zhi-20 is a medium lift helicopter produced in the Northeast of China. Its first flight was on 23 December 2013. The helicopter has a maximum takeoff weight in the range of 10 tons, can drop troops at locations of up to 3,000 ft altitude, and could operate from the Chinese aircraft carrier Liaoning.', 'node_id': '7924a5a6-7b83-4a37-b3cb-896a6fce4df9', 'score': 7.590238094329834}, {'text': 'The Eurocopter EC135 (now Airbus Helicopters H135) is a twin-engine civil light utility helicopter produced by Airbus Helicopters (formerly known as Eurocopter). It is capable of flight under instrument flight rules (IFR) and is outfitted with digital flight controls. It entered service in 1996; over a thousand aircraft have been produced to date. It is widely used by police and ambulance services and for executive transport; by 2013, more than 500 EC135s were providing helicopter emergency medical services across the world.', 'node_id': 'f3eea810-c196-4e60-80f2-df1d13c3460b', 'score': 7.373139381408691}, {'text': 'The Brantly B-2 is an American two-seat light helicopter produced by the Brantly Helicopter Corporation.', 'node_id': 'b18b88a8-b765-4b8d-af4f-768330d80721', 'score': 7.339701175689697}, {'text': 'The Bell UH-1 Iroquois (nicknamed "Huey") is a utility military helicopter powered by a single turboshaft engine, with two-blade main and tail rotors. The first member of the prolific Huey family, it was developed by Bell Helicopter to meet a United States Army\'s 1952 requirement for a medical evacuation and utility helicopter, and first flew in 1956. The UH-1 was the first turbine-powered helicopter to enter production in 1960 for the United States military, and more than 16,000 have been built since.', 'node_id': '7ce8fd6a-9cb4-455c-89b1-75676c58cab7', 'score': 6.5253705978393555}, {'text': 'MTU Aero Engines AG is a German aircraft engine manufacturer. MTU develops, manufactures and provides service support for military and civil aircraft engines. MTU Aero Engines was formerly known as MTU München.', 'node_id': '6256a593-2c79-40d1-9f6b-f3b722ea990f', 'score': 5.732956886291504}, {'text': 'The Aérospatiale (formerly Sud Aviation) SA 321 Super Frelon ("Super Hornet") is a three-engined heavy transport helicopter produced by aerospace manufacturer Sud Aviation (later Aérospatiale) of France. It held the distinction of being the most powerful helicopter to be built in Europe at one point, as well as being the world\'s fastest helicopter.', 'node_id': '4888f54a-3bfe-4f18-91b9-f3cd801e1cdd', 'score': 5.376661777496338}, {'text': 'Smith held 16 records for military aircraft in speed, endurance and distance. He was awarded the best achievement in flight Mackay Trophy twice.', 'node_id': 'fa0e2937-267b-4b53-994a-cc3755eb7c35', 'score': 5.3752570152282715}], 'consistency_check': 'CONSISTENT', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'ENTAILMENT', 'response': 'ENTAILMENT'}, 'latency': 1.147008253261447, 'vram_usage': 0.0}
