 97%|█████████▋| 485/500 [1:23:21<02:08,  8.57s/it]['Tammy Wynette'] {'response': 'The American country music singer-songwriter born in May of 1942 is Tammy Wynette. She is known for her significant contributions to country music and was one of the best-known artists in the genre. The song "The Battle," performed by George Jones, was released in 1976. Tammy Wynette sang duets with her ex-husband, George Jones, during their careers, and they were known for their collaborations. Therefore, the answer to your question is that Tammy Wynette sang a duet with her ex-husband, George Jones, in the same year that he released "The Battle."', 'query': 'What American country music singer-songwriter, born in May of 1942, sang a duet with her ex-husband the same year that he released the song "The Battle?"', 'retrieved_context': [{'text': '"The Battle" is a song by American country music artist George Jones. It was composed by Norro Wilson, George Richey, and Linda Kimball and became the title track of Jones\' 1976 LP. The song uses war as a metaphor in describing an argument and eventual reconciliation between a couple, with the woman emerging victorious and the narrator exclaiming, "Oh, what a sweet surrender!" The song begins with the sound of drums mimicking the start of a battle march.', 'node_id': '55090561-0cbc-4386-88a0-ca013fa87c74', 'score': 0.8576288223266602}, {'text': 'Loretta Lynn (née Webb; born April 14, 1932) is an American country music singer-songwriter with multiple gold albums over a career of almost 60 years. She has received numerous awards and other accolades for her groundbreaking role in country music, including awards from both the Country Music Association and Academy of Country Music as a duet partner and an individual artist. She is the most awarded female country recording artist and the only female ACM Artist of the Decade (1970s).', 'node_id': '4222c2e0-0511-48d6-acbe-766b85bce643', 'score': 0.9044911861419678}, {'text': "Tammy Wynette (born Virginia Wynette Pugh; May 5, 1942 – April 6, 1998) was an American country music singer-songwriter and one of country music's best-known artists and biggest-selling female singers.", 'node_id': 'fb467f98-6226-471a-a4c4-857abb618102', 'score': 1.0627847909927368}, {'text': 'The discography of American country artist Martina McBride consists of thirteen studio albums, one live album, four compilation albums, two video albums, three additional albums, forty five music videos, fifty one singles, sixteen other charting songs, and forty five album appearances. In 1991, she signed a recording contract with RCA Records, launching her debut studio album "The Time Has Come" in 1992. In September 1993, her second studio album "The Way That I Am" was issued.', 'node_id': '2231fd60-532c-4ef6-b423-ff21bdab918c', 'score': 1.0995556116104126}, {'text': "According to www.tootsies.net, Willie Nelson received his first songwriting gig after singing at Tootsie's. Terri Clark a Canadian-born country artist started singing at Tootsie's in 1987. and has since become an internationally known country superstar with hits such as Better Things to Do, and the Warren Zevon cover, Poor Poor Pitiful Me.", 'node_id': 'e0226bb0-75da-48e1-a01d-91b09dc654e9', 'score': 1.1127723455429077}], 'consistency_check': 'CONSISTENT', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'CONTRADICTION', 'response': 'NEUTRAL'}, 'latency': 1.174881899729371, 'vram_usage': 1.43505859375}
