['Donington, Lincolnshire'] {'response': 'Donington School F.C. was an English football club based in Donington, which is a large village and civil parish in the South Holland district of Lincolnshire, England. The club represented the Donington Grammar School and entered the first ever FA Cup in the 1871–72 season but did not compete in a match.', 'query': 'Donington School F.C. was an English football club, based in which large village and civil parish in the South Holland district of Lincolnshire, England?', 'retrieved_context': [{'text': 'Donington is a large village and civil parish in the South Holland district of Lincolnshire, England. It is situated 8 mi north from the market town of Spalding on the A152, and is bypassed by the A52. The parish includes the hamlet of Northorpe, and', 'node_id': 'd684f778-c694-4d29-98b7-e037647581bf', 'score': 24.5781192779541}, {'text': 'Quadring is a small village and civil parish in the South Holland district of Lincolnshire, England. It lies on the A152, 2 mi north-east from Gosberton, and 2 miles south-east from Donington.', 'node_id': '72a74277-0fd3-401c-b866-e951ec2deca0', 'score': 22.73213768005371}, {'text': 'Quadring Eaudike is a hamlet in the South Holland district of Lincolnshire, England. It lies approximately 1 mi east from the A152 road, and 2 mi south-east from Donington. Quadring Eaudike is within the civil parish of Quadring , a village 1 mile to the west.', 'node_id': '9b7c03a5-3da5-4d2b-957c-c7c5fcb7e9ef', 'score': 20.78723907470703}, {'text': 'Cowbit (locally pronounced "Cubbit") is a village and civil parish in the South Holland district of Lincolnshire, England. The population of the civil parish at the 2011 census was 1,220. It is situated 3 mi south from Spalding and 5 mi north from Crowland.', 'node_id': '18c41420-f610-4f9e-977a-6f75e728bdf8', 'score': 19.461904525756836}, {'text': 'Pinchbeck is a village and civil parish in the South Holland district of Lincolnshire, England. The civil parish population was 5,153 at the 2001 census, increasing to 5,455 at the 2011 census. It is situated 2 mi north from the centre of Spalding.', 'node_id': 'eabce9de-33b0-4596-b019-644b4e868ddf', 'score': 19.420644760131836}, {'text': 'Weston is a village and civil parish in the South Holland district of Lincolnshire, England. It is situated approximately 2 mi north-east from the town of Spalding. The Civil Parish also includes Weston Hills. The population of the civil parish including Austendike was at the 2011 census 2,054.', 'node_id': '802a682f-0698-4131-b8b5-302a5fe85d0f', 'score': 19.020614624023438}, {'text': 'Gedney Hill is a village and civil parish South Holland district of Lincolnshire, England. The population of the civil parish at the 2011 census was 737. It is situated close to the border of Cambridgeshire, and approximately 9 mi south-east from Spalding, 8 mi west from Wisbech and 9 miles south from Holbeach.', 'node_id': '11ed90cc-f2b6-4e22-a208-a32f9c17a7cd', 'score': 18.32124900817871}, {'text': 'Lutton (sometimes Lutton-Bourne) is a village and civil parish in the South Holland district of Lincolnshire, England. The population of the civil parish at the 2011 census was 1,261. It is situated about 4 mi south-east from the town of Holbeach. The village has been known by the alternative name of Sutton St Nicholas. The civil parish comprises the village of Lutton, with Lutton Marsh to the north-east and Lutton Garnsgate to the south-west.', 'node_id': '36a91de8-45fa-4481-881b-e587145e4d0f', 'score': 18.173187255859375}, {'text': 'Donington School F.C. was an English football club, based in Donington, Lincolnshire. The club represented the Donington Grammar School, and entered in the first ever FA Cup in 1871–72 but did not compete in a match.', 'node_id': '90e07abb-d927-49aa-9650-70244c233724', 'score': 17.911176681518555}, {'text': 'Burwell is a large village and civil parish in Cambridgeshire, England, about 10 miles (16\xa0km) north-east of Cambridge. It lies on the south-eastern edge of the Fens, a large area of flat former marshland close to sea level, covering the majority of Cambridgeshire and the South Holland district of neighbouring Lincolnshire. The fens to the west of the village are drained with the help of man-made Cambridgeshire Lode waterways, including Burwell Lode, which has been important in the growth of the village.', 'node_id': 'fdd0bed2-2ceb-4822-9a5f-2942c83136a7', 'score': 17.107452392578125}], 'consistency_check': 'MISSING', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'CONTRADICTION', 'response': 'CONTRADICTION'}, 'latency': 4.647728331387043, 'vram_usage': 0.0}
