  6%|▌         | 31/500 [05:41<1:41:08, 12.94s/it]  6%|▋         | 32/500 [05:55<1:43:08, 13.22s/it]  7%|▋         | 33/500 [05:59<1:21:13, 10.44s/it]  7%|▋         | 34/500 [06:18<1:40:27, 12.94s/it]['Pride Divide'] {'response': 'The documentary that documents the issues of the LGBT community is "Pride Divide." Directed by Paris Poirier in 1997, it specifically examines the divisions within the LGBT community, particularly between lesbians and gay men. On the other hand, "The Big Melt" is not mentioned in the provided context, so there is no information available regarding its content or focus. Therefore, based on the context, "Pride Divide" is the relevant documentary addressing LGBT community issues.', 'query': 'Which of the following documents the issues of the LGBT community: Pride Divide or The Big Melt?', 'retrieved_context': [{'text': 'Pride Divide is a 1997 documentary film directed by Paris Poirier. It examines the issues within the LGBT community relating to apparent divisions between lesbians and gay men.', 'node_id': '6f64bc56-e321-40a3-ba83-273fa673acb5', 'score': 0.7523634433746338}, {'text': 'The term "gay pride" is used to express the LGBT community\'s identity and collective strength; gay pride parades provide both a prime example of the use and a demonstration of the general meaning of the term. The LGBT community is diverse in political affiliation. Not all LGBT individuals consider themselves part of an LGBT community.', 'node_id': '699b5be9-69bb-4b4c-a491-7d4e0e9e981a', 'score': 0.7991749048233032}, {'text': 'The LGBT community or GLBT community, also referred to as the gay community, is a loosely defined grouping of lesbian, gay, bisexual, and transgender (LGBT) and LGBT-supportive people, organizations, and subcultures, united by a common culture and social movements. These communities generally celebrate pride, diversity, individuality, and sexuality. LGBT activists and sociologists see LGBT community-building as a counterbalance to heterosexism, homophobia, biphobia, transphobia, sexualism, and conformist pressures that exist in the larger society.', 'node_id': '53acca96-2efa-46f2-9681-4c867cf380e8', 'score': 0.8553224802017212}, {'text': '.lgbt is a sponsored top-level domain for the LGBT community, sponsored by Afilias. The domain name was delegated to the Root Zone on 18 July 2014. The creation of .lgbt is meant to promote diversity and LGBT businesses, and is open to LGBT businesses, organizations, and anyone wishing to reach the LGBT community.', 'node_id': '6d7e3df8-daa3-489f-857a-4eeb64bce8c4', 'score': 0.9889212846755981}, {'text': 'Baltic Pride is an annual LGBT pride parade rotating in turn between the capitals of the Baltic states; Tallinn, Riga and Vilnius. It is held in support of raising issues of tolerance and the rights of LGBT community and is supported by ILGA-Europe. Since 2009 the main organisers have been Mozaīka, the National LGBT Rights Organization LGL Lithuanian Gay League, and the Estonian LGBT Association.', 'node_id': '56a8b851-d53c-4ad8-b572-8a9fab1e36ff', 'score': 1.0363903045654297}], 'consistency_check': 'CONSISTENT', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'NEUTRAL', 'response': 'ENTAILMENT'}, 'latency': 1.2909251432865858, 'vram_usage': 1.24755859375}
