  8%|▊         | 38/500 [07:09<1:46:40, 13.85s/it]['Jonathan Stark'] {'response': "The provided context is insufficient regarding the total number of Grand Slam titles won by Henri Leconte and Jonathan Stark. However, it does mention that Henri Leconte won the French Open men's doubles title in 1984 and reached the men's singles final at the French Open in 1988, but does not specify the total number of Grand Slam titles he won. On the other hand, Jonathan Stark won two Grand Slam doubles titles: the 1994 French Open Men's Doubles and the 1995 Wimbledon Championships Mixed Doubles. Therefore, based on the information provided, it is unclear who won more Grand Slam titles overall.", 'query': 'Which tennis player won more Grand Slam titles, Henri Leconte or Jonathan Stark?', 'retrieved_context': [{'text': "Henri Leconte (born 4 July 1963) is a former French professional tennis player. He reached the men's singles final at the French Open in 1988, won the French Open men's doubles title in 1984, and helped France win the Davis Cup in 1991. Leconte's career-high singles ranking was world No. 5.", 'node_id': '1e1ebf71-07ff-45b4-8edd-0cbdc7518580', 'score': 0.5543485879898071}, {'text': "Jonathan Stark (born April 3, 1971) is a former professional tennis player from the United States. During his career he won two Grand Slam doubles titles (the 1994 French Open Men's Doubles and the 1995 Wimbledon Championships Mixed Doubles). Stark reached the World No. 1 doubles ranking in 1994.", 'node_id': 'ea1fb102-c877-4097-ac11-f8296e447819', 'score': 0.6098149418830872}, {'text': 'Kenneth Robert Rosewall {\'1\': ", \'2\': ", \'3\': \'AM, MBE\', \'4\': "} (born 2 November 1934) is a former world top-ranking amateur and professional tennis player from Australia. He won a record 23 tennis Majors including 8 Grand Slam singles titles and before the Open Era a record 15 Pro Slam titles and a record 35 Major finals overall. He won the Pro Grand Slam in 1963. Rosewall won 9 slams in doubles with a career double grand slam.', 'node_id': 'dada8c41-61c4-437f-8aea-7c2ba2aa966a', 'score': 0.8268197774887085}, {'text': 'This is a list of the main career statistics of Spanish professional tennis player, Garbiñe Muguruza. To date, Muguruza has won five WTA singles titles – most significantly the 2016 French Open and the 2017 Wimbledon Championships– and five WTA doubles titles.', 'node_id': '251edb63-3de4-4372-996e-a0940a13cb0a', 'score': 0.871990442276001}, {'text': 'Sarah Virginia Wade, (born 10 July 1945) is a former professional tennis player from Great Britain. She won three Grand Slam singles championships and four Grand Slam doubles championships, and is the only British woman in history to have won titles at all four Grand Slam tournaments. She was ranked as high as No. 2 in the world in singles, and No. 1 in the world in doubles.', 'node_id': 'f3e1ba03-831f-482d-b7c0-599cea92df36', 'score': 0.8753700852394104}], 'consistency_check': 'MISSING', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'NEUTRAL', 'response': 'ENTAILMENT'}, 'latency': 1.3636590000241995, 'vram_usage': 1.22412109375}
