  8%|▊         | 39/500 [07:36<2:17:29, 17.89s/it]['May 30, 1943'] {'response': "Fannie Lee Chaney's son, James Earl Chaney, was born on May 30, 1943. He was a civil rights worker who was murdered during the Freedom Summer in 1964. The context provides this information about his birth date and his significance in the civil rights movement.", 'query': "When was Fannie Lee Chaney's son born?", 'retrieved_context': [{'text': 'Fannie Lee Chaney (September 4, 1921 – May 22, 2007) was an American baker turned civil rights activist after her son James Chaney was murdered by the Ku Klux Klan during the 1964 Freedom Summer rides in Mississippi.', 'node_id': '5fe45f3e-2f70-44bc-bcf3-ae7848a937a9', 'score': 0.6431068181991577}, {'text': 'Darrel Lee Chaney (born March 9, 1948, in Hammond, Indiana) is an American former player/announcer in Major League Baseball who played for the Cincinnati Reds and Atlanta Braves from 1969 to 1979. In the early 1980s he worked for the Braves as an announcer along with Ernie Johnson, Skip Caray and Pete Van Wieren. He was on the Atlanta Braves Radio Network as well as WTBS-TV.', 'node_id': 'bbba80e1-6f07-4c0b-9826-b62bdab05a6a', 'score': 1.0570863485336304}, {'text': 'James Earl Chaney (May 30, 1943 – June 21, 1964), from Meridian, Mississippi, was one of three American civil rights workers who were murdered during Freedom Summer by members of the Ku Klux Klan near Philadelphia, Mississippi. The others were Andrew Goodman and Michael Schwerner from New York City.', 'node_id': 'b1636b7a-8d29-4999-b26c-0290f5ae3906', 'score': 1.1133427619934082}, {'text': 'Charlie Chan in Honolulu is a 1938 American film directed by H. Bruce Humberstone, starring Sidney Toler as the fictional Chinese-American detective Charlie Chan. The film is the first appearance of both Toler as Chan and Victor Sen Yung as "number two son" Jimmy.', 'node_id': '726d457c-c4ed-4164-bc23-d37a69288539', 'score': 1.1159831285476685}, {'text': 'Donald Lee Evans (born March 14, 1964 in Raleigh, North Carolina) is a former American football defensive end who played eight seasons in the National Football League for the Los Angeles Rams, Philadelphia Eagles, Pittsburgh Steelers, and New York Jets. He attended high school in Raleigh at Athens Drive High School, graduating in 1982.', 'node_id': 'f7a51571-f3b0-401a-a256-bb55508bda89', 'score': 1.1308053731918335}], 'consistency_check': 'CONSISTENT', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'ENTAILMENT', 'response': 'NEUTRAL'}, 'latency': 0.9871162679046392, 'vram_usage': 1.16552734375}
