 10%|█         | 50/500 [09:59<2:26:21, 19.51s/it] 10%|█         | 51/500 [10:09<2:05:16, 16.74s/it]['294,000'] {'response': "In 2012, the terminal at Erik Nielsen Whitehorse International Airport handled 294,000 passengers. This figure represents a 94% increase in passenger traffic since 2002. Therefore, the airline operating in Whitehorse, Yukon, which is Air North, Yukon's Airline, was part of this increase in passenger traffic at the airport.", 'query': 'The airline operating in Whitehorse, Yukon handled how many passengers in 2012?', 'retrieved_context': [{'text': "Air North Charter and Training Ltd., operating as Air North, Yukon's Airline is a Canadian airline based in Whitehorse, Yukon. It operates scheduled passenger and cargo flights, charter flights, and ground handling services throughout the Yukon, with regular flights to the Northwest Territories, Alaska, British Columbia, Alberta, and Ontario. Its main base is Erik Nielsen Whitehorse International Airport.", 'node_id': '21d33929-235c-469a-af67-eeabe99d148b', 'score': 0.5910111665725708}, {'text': 'Erik Nielsen Whitehorse International Airport (IATA: YXY, ICAO: CYXY) is located in Whitehorse, Yukon, Canada. It is part of the National Airports System, and is owned and operated by the Government of Yukon. The airport was renamed in honour of longtime Yukon Member of Parliament Erik Nielsen on December 15, 2008. The terminal handled 294,000 passengers in 2012, representing a 94% increase in passenger traffic since 2002. Air North is based in Whitehorse.', 'node_id': '64d9e093-8b0f-42c0-af24-7d8dd4d565e7', 'score': 0.7698285579681396}, {'text': 'The cargo division operates 91 pure freighter flights weekly. The carrier was, in 2013, the 29th and 10th largest airline in the world in terms of passenger revenue per kilometer (RPK) and freight RPK, respectively.', 'node_id': '7b2cc0e7-5b24-433c-9a7a-cc0424b4d1c7', 'score': 0.9899991750717163}, {'text': "Whitehorse Centre is an electoral district which returns a member (known as an MLA) to the Legislative Assembly of the Yukon Territory in Canada. It was created in 1992 from an amalgamation of the ridings of Whitehorse North Centre and Whitehorse South Centre and readjusted in 2002 following the dissolution of the neighbouring riding of Riverside. The riding encompasses the downtown core of the City of Whitehorse (including Marwell) between the escarpment and the Yukon River. Whitehorse Centre is home to most of Whitehorse's businesses and government offices.", 'node_id': '6de08d3f-50a2-42b3-b79a-cce81ce54115', 'score': 1.0037693977355957}, {'text': 'In 2010, Dragonair, together with its parent, Cathay Pacific, operated over 138,000 flights, carried nearly 27 million passengers and over 1.80\xa0billion kg of cargo and mail.', 'node_id': '39333c6f-b4c8-4a41-8c0c-350103caafeb', 'score': 1.0893521308898926}], 'consistency_check': 'CONSISTENT', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'ENTAILMENT', 'response': 'NEUTRAL'}, 'latency': 1.0930955857038498, 'vram_usage': 1.20068359375}
