 (mistflower).', 'node_id': 'a7a9362e-ab23-487a-9278-de24d2b4e952', 'score': 0.9648362994194031}, {'text': 'Chorisodontium aciphyllum is a species of moss found primarily on both sides of the Drake Passage. The species exhibits an extreme degree of cryptobiosis – the ability of a life form to enter a non-metabolic state, extending life indefinitely.', 'node_id': '81a23e4d-eeb7-4377-bcf2-8e22924443c6', 'score': 1.0177249908447266}, {'text': 'Huperzia is a genus of lycophyte plants, sometimes known as the firmosses or fir clubmosses. This genus was originally included in the related genus "Lycopodium", from which it differs in having undifferentiated sporangial leaves, and the sporangia not formed into apical cones. The common name "firmoss", used for some of the north temperate species, refers to their superficial resemblance to branches of fir ("Abies"), a conifer. In Australia, the epiphytic species are commonly known as tassel ferns.', 'node_id': '0cd51685-1c88-416b-9273-780f1dec007c', 'score': 1.0836186408996582}], 'consistency_check': 'MISSING', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'NEUTRAL', 'response': 'ENTAILMENT'}, 'latency': 1.337491074576974, 'vram_usage': 1.15380859375}
