['yes'] {'response': 'No, "The Watercolor" was released on November 13, 2009, while the context does not provide a specific release year for "Up." Therefore, based on the information available, it cannot be confirmed that both were released in the same year. The provided context is insufficient regarding the release year of "Up."', 'query': 'Were Up and The Watercolor released in the same year?', 'retrieved_context': [{'text': '"The Watercolor (Tr: Suluboya)" is a 2009 Turkish animated film, directed by Cihat Hazardağlı. The film went on nationwide general release on November 13, 2009.', 'node_id': '3142ab62-1bc3-4a8f-9a96-4e40f653ab44', 'score': 1.098404884338379}, {'text': "by Waters' band Contribution in 2004.", 'node_id': '8df862e1-b2ff-4c20-9060-84ec920ee78b', 'score': 1.1194509267807007}, {'text': 'The EP was released on the 6th of May and features 5 songs from her debut album, as well as a cover of Canadian singer Joni Mitchell\'s "A Case of You". In 2015, Aplin released her second studio album entitled "Light Up the Dark". "Light Up the Dark" debuted at number 14 on the UK Albums Chart.', 'node_id': '3d870243-d7f4-4565-a0e6-da70bc4a286f', 'score': 1.1404460668563843}, {'text': 'Production began in May 2000 and ended in August 2000, and took place largely on location in London and the Home Counties. The film premiered on 4 April 2001 in the UK and was released to theatres on 13 April 2001 simultaneously in the UK and in the US.', 'node_id': '309c7c8b-0970-4d44-96f4-6a1a18346bd3', 'score': 1.1482653617858887}, {'text': 'Two singles were released from the album, "Round & Round" and "A Year Without Rain".', 'node_id': 'df391de7-b514-4b3c-99c7-533495a37b2b', 'score': 1.1585432291030884}, {'text': 'A live version was also included on their 2016 album "Playing Favorites".', 'node_id': 'db37a864-9046-4f35-8680-26295c699ac8', 'score': 1.1655187606811523}, {'text': 'The second single from the album, "Naturally", reached the top thirty in the United States, the top twenty in New Zealand, Canada and Germany and the top ten in both Ireland and the United Kingdom. The song has also been certified platinum in the United States and Canada. Their second album, "A Year Without Rain" was released on September 17, 2010. It debuted on the US "Billboard" 200 at number four and was certified Gold by the RIAA in January 2011.', 'node_id': '533af288-0817-499b-b837-035c97655e58', 'score': 1.1746909618377686}, {'text': 'The band released their third album "Evolution" on March 15, 2011, with that album still working its way into and up the charts.', 'node_id': '8f5a70b6-7a8f-42cb-bf27-f4f5e2475247', 'score': 1.18917977809906}, {'text': 'Their debut album "Take Your Light" was released in 2011, to positive reviews.', 'node_id': 'b3c8b92a-2710-4699-840e-5afc35452c94', 'score': 1.2018935680389404}, {'text': 'Entitled “Jetpack Soundtrack”, this Lionize record was released on February 18th, 2014 in North America, April 11th, 2014 in Europe, and February 14th, 2014 in the UK. The Lionize signing marks the label’s first signing of an independent artist to Weathermaker Music.', 'node_id': '28d767b4-643f-4269-bc51-649f107310cf', 'score': 1.2197637557983398}], 'consistency_check': 'CONSISTENT', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'CONTRADICTION', 'response': 'ENTAILMENT'}, 'latency': 5.436408776789904, 'vram_usage': 1.16552734375}
