 15%|█▌        | 76/500 [15:21<1:17:39, 10.99s/it]['The Joshua Tree'] {'response': 'The provided context is insufficient regarding the specific album from which the cover song "I Still Haven\'t Found What I\'m Looking For" by The Chimes, featuring Pauline Henry as the vocalist, originated.', 'query': 'Pauline Henry was known as the vocalist of a very popular cover song. Which album was this song from?', 'retrieved_context': [{'text': 'Pauline Henry (born 29 January 1961) is a British Jamaican recording artist. She was the vocalist in the Scottish band The Chimes, best known for their 1990 cover version of U2\'s "I Still Haven\'t Found What I\'m Looking For", between 1988 and 1991. Following her departure from the group, Henry embarked on a solo career, and achieved five UK top 40 singles between 1993 and 1996.', 'node_id': 'c901c912-6eda-4bac-8bc1-8f974881a33e', 'score': 0.9188188314437866}, {'text': 'The Chimes were a successful dance music trio. Pauline Henry (born in Jamaica) with Mike Peden and James Locke from Edinburgh, in Scotland. They are best known for their hits "Heaven" and a remake of U2\'s "I Still Haven\'t Found What I\'m Looking For," which became a UK Top Ten hit.', 'node_id': 'e4fd7132-2e55-44a0-bfff-b1f24b28a4fb', 'score': 1.0190587043762207}, {'text': 'Dolly Parton\'s cover of the 1965 Petula Clark hit "Downtown" was the album\'s second single. The title song was originally a hit for The Platters in 1956.', 'node_id': '445f1738-a8f5-416a-88bc-d8cdfd98fb27', 'score': 1.069058895111084}, {'text': '"Sarah" is a pop song released in 1979 by Irish rock group Thin Lizzy, included on their album, "". The song was written by the band\'s frontman Phil Lynott and guitarist Gary Moore about Lynott\'s newborn daughter. The song was also issued as a single, and appeared on several compilation albums including "". The song was never performed live by Thin Lizzy, but it was adopted as a live favourite by Lynott\'s post-Thin Lizzy project, Grand Slam, and featured on "Live in Sweden 1983", a recording of Lynott\'s solo band.', 'node_id': '94718881-9d32-48a4-8634-2ddd7a11254f', 'score': 1.0714281797409058}, {'text': 'In popular music, a cover version or cover song, or simply cover, is a new performance or recording of a previously recorded, commercially released song by someone other than the original artist or composer.', 'node_id': '66499707-86e5-406f-b9d9-44102f56e9da', 'score': 1.0944006443023682}], 'consistency_check': 'CONFLICT', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'ENTAILMENT', 'response': 'ENTAILMENT'}, 'latency': 0.8564917147159576, 'vram_usage': 1.27099609375}
