 17%|█▋        | 84/500 [17:24<1:56:35, 16.82s/it]['La Fea Mas Bella'] {'response': 'The provided context is insufficient regarding the specific roles of the Mexican actor Jaime Camil, including his role as Fernando Mendiola. The context mentions that Jaime Camil hosted the 32nd TCA Awards, but it does not provide information about the specific works or roles he is known for.', 'query': 'The 32nd TCA Awards were hosted by a  Mexican actor best known for his roles as Fernando Mendiola in what?', 'retrieved_context': [{'text': 'The 32nd TCA Awards were held on August 6, 2016, in a ceremony hosted by Jaime Camil at The Beverly Hilton in Beverly Hills, California. The nominees were announced by the Television Critics Association on June 22, 2016.', 'node_id': 'c13b1f45-ae8c-4197-81d6-f0cfdc4eb4c0', 'score': 0.8644253015518188}, {'text': 'The 22nd TCA Awards were presented by the Television Critics Association. Mary Lynn Rajskub hosted the ceremony on July 23, 2006 at the Huntington Hotel and Spa in Pasadena, California.', 'node_id': 'e64085ee-5630-404d-aaab-8124271db91a', 'score': 0.9085389971733093}, {'text': 'Mario Fortino Alfonso Moreno Reyes, known casually as Mario Moreno, and known professionally as Cantinflas (August 12, 1911 – April 20, 1993), was a Mexican comic film actor, producer, and screenwriter and an iconic figure in Mexico and Latin America. He often portrayed impoverished "campesinos" or a peasant of "pelado" origin. The character came to be associated with the national identity of Mexico, and allowed Cantinflas to establish a long, successful film career that included a foray into Hollywood.', 'node_id': '4d00002e-2533-42b8-a415-ab0fd5b7c982', 'score': 0.955960750579834}, {'text': 'Fernando Fernández "El Crooner de México" (1916–1999) was a Mexican actor and singer. He was born on November 9, 1916, in Monterrey, Mexico, and died in Mexico City, Mexico, on November 24, 1999. Fernando was the son of Eloisa Reyes. He was brother of the famous film director Emilio Fernández and actor Jaime Fernández. He was married to singer Lupita Palomera, who died in 2008. Fernando Fernández was known as "the Crooner of Mexico."', 'node_id': '0bab1cef-4752-4b39-b0e2-bd5a82addfbe', 'score': 0.9585041403770447}, {'text': 'The 2nd TCA Awards were presented by the Television Critics Association. The ceremony was held on June 10, 1986, at the Beverly Wilshire Hotel in Los Angeles, Calif.', 'node_id': '9e79ff8f-b924-4815-bb32-023293f85718', 'score': 0.9830183982849121}], 'consistency_check': 'MISSING', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'NEUTRAL', 'response': 'ENTAILMENT'}, 'latency': 1.4332544580101967, 'vram_usage': 1.30615234375}
