Ohio, Metropolitan Statistical Area, which encompasses ten counties. With a population of 2,021,632, it is Ohio's third-largest metropolitan area.", 'node_id': '04ed9853-ca6a-4929-8eed-f5d9fecfed37', 'score': 1.148592472076416}, {'text': 'The most populous city in the country is the capital, Mexico City, with a population of 8.9 million (2016), and its metropolitan area is also the most populated with 20.1 million (2010). Approximately 50% of the population lives in one of the 55 large metropolitan areas in the country. In total, about 78.84% of the population of the country lives in urban areas, meaning that only 21.16% live in rural areas.', 'node_id': 'af54de07-b855-4b1b-a8b7-e78370d9eefb', 'score': 1.2560421228408813}], 'consistency_check': 'MISSING', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'NEUTRAL', 'response': 'ENTAILMENT'}, 'latency': 1.00329914316535, 'vram_usage': 1.30615234375}
