-a631-44a6-9635-0343d8f5bc6e', 'score': 1.066979169845581}, {'text': 'The district borders Merseyside, Warrington and Cheshire West and Chester. The borough straddles the River Mersey – the area to the north (including Widnes) is historically part of Lancashire, that to the south (including Runcorn) part of Cheshire.', 'node_id': '98853782-4730-42f5-997f-09fde8812123', 'score': 1.1231675148010254}, {'text': "Haslingden is a town in Rossendale, Lancashire, England. It is 19 mi north of Manchester. The name means 'valley of the hazels'. At the time of the 2001 census the town had a population of 16,849.", 'node_id': 'a4b7b5f3-78ee-43bd-b641-45be39ee2a31', 'score': 1.1609315872192383}], 'consistency_check': 'MISSING', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'NEUTRAL', 'response': 'ENTAILMENT'}, 'latency': 0.7592463735491037, 'vram_usage': 1.20068359375}
