 27%|██▋       | 137/500 [26:59<1:26:40, 14.33s/it]['Bart Conner'] {'response': "The provided context is insufficient regarding the husband of Nadia Elena Comăneci, the first Olympic gymnast to be awarded a perfect score of 10.0. While it mentions her achievements and background, it does not provide information about her marital status or her husband's identity.", 'query': 'Who was the husband of the first olympic gymnast to be awarded a perfect score of 10.0?', 'retrieved_context': [{'text': 'Nadia Elena Comăneci (] ; born November 12, 1961) is a Romanian Olympic gold medalist, who at the age of 14 in the Olympic games during the 1976 Olympics in Montreal, became the first gymnast to be awarded a perfect score of 10.0. In all, she received six more perfect 10s in Montreal, as well as three gold medals. Four years later, she won two gold medals at the 1980 Olympics in Moscow. She won nine Olympic medals and four World Championship medals during her career.', 'node_id': '98c63fd7-1c09-43fd-b287-49a3a6eafa1d', 'score': 0.5620647072792053}, {'text': 'She medalled in every single World Championships meet, Olympic Games and European Championships between 1991 and 1996, and is only the third female gymnast ever, after Larisa Latynina and Věra Čáslavská, to win at least one World Championships or Olympic title on all four events. Miloșovici was also the last gymnast along with Lu Li to ever receive the perfect mark of 10.0 in an Olympic competition and the last to receive the benchmark score of 9.95 at the World Championships.', 'node_id': '8045ec18-8925-4f08-b235-f488268fcc2e', 'score': 0.8565584421157837}, {'text': 'Irma Pezzia Haubold (November 20, 1908 – April 4, 1996) was an American artistic gymnast. She competed at the 1936 Summer Olympics and placed fifth with the team. She was married to a fellow Olympic gymnast Frank Haubold. They were the first married couple of compete in the same Olympics.', 'node_id': '3c29ab2d-c853-478a-884a-160f8643aa10', 'score': 0.8898871541023254}, {'text': 'men’s gymnastics team in olympic history. In addition to the team gold medal, he earned an individual bronze medal on the pommel horse. In 2005, he was inducted into the United States Olympic Hall of Fame.', 'node_id': 'a422176a-38df-499f-8877-77ce23c318af', 'score': 0.9091144800186157}, {'text': 'Lavinia Corina Miloșovici (born 21 October 1976) is a retired Romanian artistic gymnast. An exceptionally successful athlete on the international competition circuit, Miloșovici, also known as "Milo" in the gymnastics community, is considered to be one of Romania\'s top gymnasts of the 1990s and one of the most prolific female all-around gymnasts of the decade, earning a total 19 World Championships or Olympic medals in a span of six years.', 'node_id': '5a2796eb-ba58-45da-ab81-f76d872330b3', 'score': 0.9521499872207642}], 'consistency_check': 'CONSISTENT', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'NEUTRAL', 'response': 'ENTAILMENT'}, 'latency': 0.9065841604024172, 'vram_usage': 1.25927734375}
