way, that runs from Carinthia\'s Möll valley into the Reißeck Group, a small mountain range in southern Austria. It comprises the Reisseck Funicular and the Reisseck Mountain Railway (a narrow gauge railway).', 'node_id': '0b655ef4-4812-4f0f-842f-d4d513d48eb2', 'score': 0.8923192620277405}, {'text': 'In the Czech Republic the line is known today as the "Moldavská horská dráha" ("Moldau Mountain Railway") or "Krušnohorská železnice" ("Ore Mountain Railway").', 'node_id': 'a07a0a8e-2f9a-4182-bf1f-331f95188b87', 'score': 0.9177934527397156}, {'text': 'The Most–Moldava railway is a branch line in Czech Republic, which was originally built and operated by the Prague-Dux Railway. The line, formerly known as the"Teplitz Semmering Railway" ("Teplitzer Semmeringbahn") runs from Most ("Brüx") over the Ore Mountains to Moldava ("Moldau") and used to have a junction with the Nossen-Moldau railway there in Saxony until 1945.', 'node_id': '0ecb39e4-6556-45d2-bb58-e837274cdc68', 'score': 1.009774923324585}], 'consistency_check': 'MISSING', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'ENTAILMENT', 'response': 'NEUTRAL'}, 'latency': 0.9062782246619463, 'vram_usage': 1.39990234375}
