['Robert Manoogian Jr. (January 4, 1918 – April 3, 2002) was an American professional wrestler'] {'response': "The provided context is insufficient regarding whether Bobby Managoff was a record producer. It mentions that George Avakian is an American record producer known for his work with Columbia Records and various notable jazz musicians. However, it only describes Bobby Managoff as a professional wrestler known for his work with the National Wrestling Alliance in the 1940s, without any mention of him being a record producer. Therefore, while George Avakian is indeed a record producer, there is no information provided about Bobby Managoff's involvement in record production.", 'query': 'Are George Avakian and Bobby Managoff both record producers?', 'retrieved_context': [{'text': 'Trombone For Two is a 1956 album by jazz trombonists J. J. Johnson and Kai Winding ("Jay and Kai"). It was the first of five albums that Winding and Johnson recorded for Columbia Records (CL 742). George Avakian produced the recording sessions, which took place on June 23 and 24, 1955.', 'node_id': '16b9538d-d2bf-4d84-be97-b9f49e453e0c', 'score': 7.492195129394531}, {'text': "Bill Haley and His Comets is the title of the tenth album of rock and roll recordings by Bill Haley & His Comets. Released in April 1960, it was the band's first album release for Warner Bros. Records, following their departure from Decca Records at the end of 1959. The recordings were produced by George Avakian, who succeeded Haley's Decca producer, Milt Gabler.", 'node_id': '2e7476fc-8d6d-4b8c-841c-640e7bb0a2dc', 'score': 7.350141525268555}, {'text': 'Robert Manoogian Jr. (January 4, 1918 – April 3, 2002) was an American professional wrestler of Armenian descent who was best known for his work with National Wrestling Alliance in the 1940s as Bobby Managoff.', 'node_id': '87468a21-639d-4d17-bb95-4f9039452ab8', 'score': 7.325198173522949}, {'text': "Jazz on a Summer's Day (1960) is a concert film set at the 1958 Newport Jazz Festival in Rhode Island, directed by commercial and fashion photographer Bert Stern. The Columbia Records jazz producer, George Avakian, was the musical director of the film.", 'node_id': '5bc19f5b-541b-4fc3-8875-0b36b1bb8735', 'score': 7.289294719696045}, {'text': 'George Avakian (Armenian: Գևորգ Ավագյան ; Russian: Геворк Авакян ; born March 15, 1919) is an American record producer and executive known particularly for his work with Columbia Records, and his production of albums by Louis Armstrong, Miles Davis and other notable jazz musicians.', 'node_id': 'c0e035d0-a683-4719-a878-bc4b2d4e58e8', 'score': 7.270410537719727}, {'text': 'Haley\'s Juke Box: Songs of the Bill Haley Generation (often listed in reference books as "Bill Haley\'s Jukebox"), is the eleventh studio album by Bill Haley & His Comets. Released by Warner Bros. Records in the summer of 1960, the album was produced by George Avakian.', 'node_id': '71375e6e-f7c8-4a76-a021-68b4436e1a5e', 'score': 7.021324157714844}, {'text': 'Expectations is a 1972 album by the pianist, saxophonist and composer Keith Jarrett, released on Columbia Records. In addition to Jarrett, musicians on the recording include Dewey Redman (tenor saxophone), Charlie Haden (bass), Paul Motian (drums), Sam Brown (guitar), Airto Moreira (percussion), as well as brass and string sections whose members are not credited in the album information. "Expectations" was produced by George Avakian.', 'node_id': 'f53aec99-4603-46b7-a008-6536c17ebe53', 'score': 6.409844398498535}, {'text': 'The sextet was founded and managed by Dick Voigt, and counted as members the later-legendary trombonist Roswell Rudd, bassists Buell Neidlinger (succeeded by Bob Morgan), cornetist and cartoonist Lee Lorenz, clarinetist Pete Williams (who was succeeded by Leroy Sam Parkins) and drummer Lyman "House" Drake (who was succeeded by Steve Little). With the help of the producer and Yale alumnus George Avakian, the band recorded an album for Columbia Records in 1955.', 'node_id': 'dc8f6e76-717f-4694-8ef9-8c967dde7d52', 'score': 6.109318733215332}, {'text': 'Columbia CD released the album on CD in 1986 in a much altered form, with alternative versions in place of many of the original songs, but restored the original with its 1997 re-issue, which also included additional tracks: a brief interview by the producer, George Avakian, with W. C. Handy; a joke told by Louis Armstrong; and several rehearsal versions of the songs.', 'node_id': 'ddf17b68-4cb8-4888-8224-47ff68f760f9', 'score': 5.333808422088623}, {'text': 'Gorgeous George is the third solo studio album by Scottish musician Edwyn Collins. The album was recorded at New River in London, with Collins acting as the producer.', 'node_id': '7164a24b-7083-4cc3-b4fa-44dde0a25cda', 'score': 4.726380825042725}], 'consistency_check': 'CONSISTENT', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'NEUTRAL', 'response': 'ENTAILMENT'}, 'latency': 1.1725369840860367, 'vram_usage': 0.0}
