 38%|███▊      | 192/500 [34:31<44:52,  8.74s/it] 39%|███▊      | 193/500 [34:35<37:18,  7.29s/it] 39%|███▉      | 194/500 [34:40<33:20,  6.54s/it] 39%|███▉      | 195/500 [34:53<44:33,  8.77s/it] 39%|███▉      | 196/500 [35:05<48:26,  9.56s/it]['no'] {'response': 'No, only Juniper belongs to the cypress family Cupressaceae. The provided context specifies that junipers are coniferous plants in the genus Juniperus of the cypress family Cupressaceae. However, there is no mention of Indigofera in the context, and it is not part of the cypress family. Therefore, the answer is no; only Juniper is part of the Cupressaceae family, while Indigofera does not belong to this family.', 'query': 'Do both Juniper and Indigofera belong to the cypress family Cupressaceae?', 'retrieved_context': [{'text': 'Junipers are coniferous plants in the genus Juniperus of the cypress family Cupressaceae. Depending on taxonomic viewpoint, between 50 and 67 species of juniper are widely distributed throughout the Northern Hemisphere, from the Arctic, south to tropical Africa, from Ziarat, Pakistan east to eastern Tibet in the Old World, and in the mountains of Central America. The highest-known Juniper forest occurs at an altitude of 16000 ft in south-eastern Tibet and the northern Himalayas, creating one of the highest tree-lines on earth.', 'node_id': 'b547f168-c55f-4b40-a77b-a72a95e5ce54', 'score': 0.623573899269104}, {'text': 'Dwarf cypress is a common name used for several plants in the conifer family Cupressaceae (cypress family)', 'node_id': '80719ca3-f0ad-4b4f-98db-19233fb2e848', 'score': 0.6474757194519043}, {'text': 'Chamaecyparis, common names cypress or false cypress (to distinguish it from related cypresses), is a genus of conifers in the cypress family Cupressaceae, native to eastern Asia (Japan + Taiwan) and to the western and eastern margins of the United States. The name is derived from the Greek "khamai", meaning ground, and "kuparissos" for cypress.', 'node_id': 'df64da66-14e0-4767-9456-fc473350411e', 'score': 0.8442174196243286}, {'text': 'Cryptomeria (literally "hidden parts") is a monotypic genus of conifer in the cypress family Cupressaceae, formerly belonging to the family Taxodiaceae. It includes only one species, Cryptomeria japonica (syn. "Cupressus japonica" L.f.). It is endemic to Japan, where it is known as sugi (Japanese: 杉 ). The tree is called Japanese sugi pine or Japanese red-cedar in English.', 'node_id': 'f105444e-698c-4cf5-bf7f-2696a8a2fffc', 'score': 0.9104673862457275}, {'text': 'Callitris columellaris is a species of coniferous tree in the family Cupressaceae (cypress family), native to most of Australia. Common names include White Cypress-pine, Murray River Cypress-pine, and Northern Cypress-pine. "Callitris columellaris" has been naturalised in Hawaii and in southern Florida.', 'node_id': '79274a65-25a4-4925-8f27-346df412044e', 'score': 0.9135068655014038}], 'consistency_check': 'CONSISTENT', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'NEUTRAL', 'response': 'ENTAILMENT'}, 'latency': 1.599978569895029, 'vram_usage': 1.20068359375}
