 40%|████      | 202/500 [36:02<45:00,  9.06s/it]['Reggie Yates'] {'response': 'The host of The Voice UK who was in "Doctor Who" is Reggie Yates. He is known for his role as Leo Jones in "Doctor Who." In addition to his work on "The Voice UK," where he co-hosted the second series alongside Holly Willoughby, Yates has had a diverse career in television and radio, presenting various shows for the BBC. His involvement in "Doctor Who" adds to his credentials as a television presenter and actor.', 'query': 'What host of The Voice UK was in "Doctor Who"?', 'retrieved_context': [{'text': 'The "Doctor Who" Prom 2010 was a concert showcasing incidental music from the British science fiction television series "Doctor Who", along with classical music, performed as part of the BBC\'s Proms series of concerts. The concert was performed on 24 and 25 July 2010 at the Royal Albert Hall in London, and was hosted by actors Matt Smith, who portrays the Doctor, and Karen Gillan and Arthur Darvill, who play his companions, Amy Pond and Rory Williams.', 'node_id': '26795f23-2ada-4acd-bc72-93cdae3b6c34', 'score': 0.7606581449508667}, {'text': "The Voice UK is a British television music competition to find new singing talent. The second series was hosted by Holly Willoughby and Reggie Yates on BBC One and started on 30 March 2013. On 13 November 2012, it was confirmed that all four coaches from last year would return. The show's Blind Auditions moved to MediaCityUK in Salford, Greater Manchester.", 'node_id': '5d61e1e3-709f-4216-83af-b03f772e1b29', 'score': 0.7759663462638855}, {'text': 'The Eleventh Doctor is an incarnation of the Doctor, the protagonist of the BBC science fiction television programme "Doctor Who". He is played by Matt Smith, in three series as well as seven specials, over an almost four-year-long period. As with previous incarnations of the Doctor, the character has also appeared in other "Doctor Who" multimedia.', 'node_id': 'ac4de41e-b520-42e5-b2dd-89063ae199c8', 'score': 0.8075010180473328}, {'text': 'Reggie Yates (born 31 May 1983) is a British actor, television presenter and radio DJ, best known from his roles as Rastamouse, Leo Jones in "Doctor Who", and for his work at the BBC in radio and television - presenting various shows for BBC Radio 1 with Fearne Cotton – as well as hosting the ITV2 reality show "Release the Hounds" from 2013 until 2017.', 'node_id': '99f8c4a9-8380-4c71-8416-33744100805e', 'score': 0.9530668258666992}, {'text': 'Dr. Tony Gardner (born 10 January 1964) is an English actor and doctor. He qualified as a doctor at Guy\'s Hospital in 1987, then as a general practitioner in 1993. He combined medicine and comedy during the 1990s as half of the award-winning comedy duo "Struck Off and Die" with Phil Hammond.', 'node_id': '9ad2c04a-8ded-40f4-b0bc-7eb8fbc36bb9', 'score': 0.9744166135787964}], 'consistency_check': 'CONFLICT', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'ENTAILMENT', 'response': 'ENTAILMENT'}, 'latency': 1.1599172037094831, 'vram_usage': 1.17724609375}
