['Showbox'] {'response': 'The provided context is insufficient regarding the company that released Lee Il-hyung\'s first feature film "A Violent Prosecutor."', 'query': "Lee Il-hyung's first feature film was released by which company ?", 'retrieved_context': [{'text': 'Lee Il-hyung is a South Korean film director and screenwriter. Prior to directing his first feature film "A Violent Prosecutor" (2016), Lee is an assistant director on films, such as "The Moonlight of Seoul" (2008), "My Way" (2011) and "" (2014), and commercial films.', 'node_id': '7758f281-220a-4c64-8254-d421a1952c27', 'score': 7.0020432}, {'text': 'Chang Mi-hee (born December 8, 1958) is a South Korean actress active since 1976. She was born Lee Yun-hui in Seoul, South Korea in 1957. Chang debuted as an actress in 1976 as starring in "Seong Chun-hyang jeon" directed by Park Tae-won and TBC TV drama, "Haenyeo Dang-sil" (Sea Woman Dang-sil).', 'node_id': '2920b9fc-1f95-47c4-aeb1-419f75309b8a', 'score': -2.2434056}, {'text': 'In 2010, he was named the "New Generation Producer" at the 18th Korean Culture Entertainment Awards, and in 2011 he was named as one of the most influential figures in the South Korean music industry by OSEN. Lee has recently started his own label, AB Entertainment, in which he has debuted his own girl group named EXID.', 'node_id': '0194bbb3-ea48-4514-95d3-03fcb3b2ec7f', 'score': -3.2894719}], 'consistency_check': 'CONSISTENT', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'CONTRADICTION', 'response': 'CONTRADICTION'}, 'latency': 0.9194413609802723, 'vram_usage': 9.0830078125}
