 48%|████▊     | 239/500 [41:01<31:08,  7.16s/it]['American'] {'response': "The provided context is insufficient regarding James Henry Miller's wife and her nationality.", 'query': " What nationality was James Henry Miller's wife?", 'retrieved_context': [{'text': 'June Miller (January 7 or 28, 1902 – February 1, 1979) was the much-written-about second wife of Henry Miller.', 'node_id': '480b7bb5-4c28-43da-9c6f-a5bca9c7331e', 'score': 0.5505683422088623}, {'text': 'James Henry Miller (born 30 May 1919) is a former Australian rules footballer in the Victorian Football League (VFL).', 'node_id': '693cb1d3-bb06-4e89-b49c-ec46d6bc7895', 'score': 0.6771272420883179}, {'text': 'James Henry Miller (25 January 1915 – 22 October 1989), better known by his stage name Ewan MacColl, was an English folk singer, songwriter, communist, labour activist, actor, poet, playwright and record producer.', 'node_id': '817a5183-17d5-4789-83cd-c15fc0973c83', 'score': 0.8594984412193298}, {'text': 'The Henry Miller Memorial Library is a nonprofit arts center, bookstore, and performance venue, championing the late writer, artist, and Big Sur resident Henry Miller, as well as many other, both living and dead, creative individuals living in or near Big Sur, California. Henry Miller’s friend Emil White built the house that is now the Library in the mid-1960s. After Miller died, in 1980, Emil decided to maintain his property as a memorial to his friend and as a gallery where local artists could show their work.', 'node_id': 'b3fd5094-47e2-4950-94bd-80433ed1a549', 'score': 0.9677741527557373}, {'text': 'Joseph Hillis Miller Jr. (born March 5, 1928) is an American literary critic who has been heavily influenced by—and who has heavily influenced—deconstruction.', 'node_id': '5b687bf6-31e5-4fdd-a8ea-97b4f9e970ed', 'score': 1.0052809715270996}], 'consistency_check': 'CONFLICT', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'NEUTRAL', 'response': 'NEUTRAL'}, 'latency': 0.6897180434316397, 'vram_usage': 1.14208984375}
