['Max Gail'] {'response': 'The actor who appeared in the film "D.C. Cab" and also had a role in the TV series "Barney Miller" is Ron Carey. In "D.C. Cab," he played a character named Arnie, while in "Barney Miller," he portrayed the ambitious NYPD Police Officer Carl Levitt. Carey was known for his recurring role in the latter series, appearing in the last six of its eight seasons.', 'query': 'What actor in the film D.C. Cab also had a role in the TV series Barney Miller?', 'retrieved_context': [{'text': 'Detective Phil Fish is a fictional NYPD detective in the TV series "Barney Miller" and later in the spin off series "Fish". He was played by Abe Vigoda.', 'node_id': 'e5f86555-4385-472d-86ca-947918df479e', 'score': 10.007619857788086}, {'text': 'Maxwell Trowbridge "Max" Gail Jr. (born April 5, 1943) is an American actor who has starred in stage, television, and film roles. He most notably portrayed the role of Detective Stan "Wojo" Wojciehowicz on the television sitcom "Barney Miller".', 'node_id': 'f5b98f39-b594-479c-ad90-8317e3bb3094', 'score': 9.62042236328125}, {'text': 'She has also been in "The Last Unicorn" (voice), Rankin/Bass "The Return of the King", "Americathon", the miniseries "East of Eden", and guest roles on various TV shows such as "Barnaby Jones", "Barney Miller", "Starsky and Hutch", and "Happy Days" as Fonzie\'s ex-fiancée Maureen Johnson, a.k.a. "The Lone Stripper", in the Season 2 episode of the series titled "Fonzie\'s Getting Married" (episode #13).', 'node_id': '7149955a-f083-4979-9910-860371c0e333', 'score': 8.973836898803711}, {'text': 'Jack Soo (October 28, 1917 – January 11, 1979) was a Japanese American actor. He is best known for his role as Detective Nick Yemana on the television sitcom "Barney Miller".', 'node_id': '179ba9f2-2fa0-4e11-9ec6-356bdc793be1', 'score': 8.942079544067383}, {'text': 'Steve Landesberg (November 23, 1936December 20, 2010) was an American actor, comedian, and voice actor known for his role as the erudite, unflappable police detective Arthur P. Dietrich on the ABC sitcom "Barney Miller", for which he was nominated for three Emmy Awards.', 'node_id': 'd214a35e-93ef-4a97-a2d7-03f0cdc99097', 'score': 8.61428165435791}, {'text': 'Ronald Joseph Cicenia (December 11, 1935 – January 16, 2007), known as Ron Carey, was an American film and television actor. The 5 ft actor was best known for playing ambitious NYPD Police Officer Carl Levitt on TV\'s "Barney Miller", in which he was almost always surrounded by male actors (and sometimes female guest stars) who stood at least 4 in taller. The series\' stars (Hal Linden, Max Gail, Abe Vigoda, Ron Glass, Steve Landesberg) all stood 6 ft or more.', 'node_id': '76d42a50-ebfb-4ea0-98fe-cbb12c1158c1', 'score': 8.559542655944824}, {'text': 'Shelby Fredrick "Sheb" Wooley (April 10, 1921 – September 16, 2003) was a character actor and singer, best known for his 1958 novelty song "The Purple People Eater." He played Ben Miller, brother of Frank Miller, in the film "High Noon"; played Travis Cobb in "The Outlaw Josey Wales"; and also had a co-starring role as scout Pete Nolan in the television series "Rawhide."', 'node_id': '036a269e-6342-4dd4-8fd6-2db935c4d168', 'score': 8.513301849365234}, {'text': 'He was also nominated for a Golden Globe Award for Best Actor – Television Series Musical or Comedy for his role in the TV series "Graves" (2016–present).', 'node_id': '544add41-3c50-471c-9736-b48bcdab74b9', 'score': 8.235116004943848}, {'text': 'Jim Moody (born September 25, 1949 in Portsmouth, Virginia) is a television and film character actor. He played the tough-talking counselor/teacher Gene Daniels in "Bad Boys". His first feature film role was in the 1980 hit film "Fame", in which he played Mr. Farrell, a drama teacher. Jim starred in the 1983 comedy film "D.C. Cab" as Arnie, a member of the rival cab company, Emerald Cab.', 'node_id': '0ba6c1ec-e73c-4920-8021-d7b7e9d015b7', 'score': 7.772692680358887}, {'text': 'Carey appeared in the recurring role for the last six of the eight seasons of "Barney Miller"\' s run. He first appeared on the show as a criminal, Angelo Molinari (aka The Mole), in Season 2, Episode 22.', 'node_id': '62f3caeb-607c-4a16-b602-ce8d431aff82', 'score': 7.333914756774902}], 'consistency_check': 'CONFLICT', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'ENTAILMENT', 'response': 'CONTRADICTION'}, 'latency': 1.4042222667485476, 'vram_usage': 0.0}
