 54%|█████▍    | 270/500 [45:41<39:44, 10.37s/it]['Peter Chelsom'] {'response': 'The director of the 2001 American romantic comedy film written by Marc Klein, in which Lucy Gordon had a small role, is Peter Chelsom. This film is titled "Serendipity" and stars John Cusack and Kate Beckinsale. Lucy Gordon\'s involvement in this film is part of her early acting career, which included various roles in both independent films and larger productions.', 'query': 'Who was the director of the 2001 American romantic comedy film written by Marc Klein in which Lucy Gordon had a small role?', 'retrieved_context': [{'text': 'Lucy Gordon (22 May 1980 – 20 May 2009) was an English actress and model. She became a face of CoverGirl in 1997 before starting an acting career. Her first film was "Perfume" in 2001 before going on to have small roles in "Spider-Man 3", "Serendipity" and "The Four Feathers". Gordon had played the actress and singer Jane Birkin in the film "", a biopic of singer-songwriter Serge Gainsbourg.', 'node_id': 'fd2d63fa-b392-404b-9556-cbebb8507f18', 'score': 1.0338257551193237}, {'text': 'Serendipity is a 2001 American romantic comedy film directed by Peter Chelsom, written by Marc Klein, and starring John Cusack and Kate Beckinsale. The music score was composed by Alan Silvestri.', 'node_id': '3f79529c-b4d8-4fbf-9e99-48e28ea1b93c', 'score': 1.1115702390670776}, {'text': "See This Movie is a 2004 comedy film written by David M. Rosenthal and Joseph Matthew Smith, and directed by Rosenthal. The film stars Seth Meyers and John Cho, and also features Jessica Paré, Jim Piddock, and Jessalyn Gilsig, with cameo appearances by Patton Oswalt, Miguel Arteta, and the film's executive producers Chris Weitz and Paul Weitz.", 'node_id': '8237ae40-7f33-47f6-8c01-e4b6aa5bf6c7', 'score': 1.1465188264846802}, {'text': 'She later appeared in several independent films and short subjects as well as the thriller "Trapped" (2002) alongside Charlize Theron and Kevin Bacon, and "Julie Johnson" (2001), for which she received an award for Best Actress at Los Angeles\' gay and lesbian Outfest film festival.', 'node_id': 'cef5050f-9341-4e8e-a430-444cdde4b9e0', 'score': 1.1901030540466309}, {'text': 'We Married Margo is a 2000 American independent comedy film directed by J. David Shapiro and co-written by Shapiro and William Dozier. The film tells a story of two friends who were married to the same woman and is loosely based on real events in that Shapiro and Dozier actually met after dating the same woman named Margaux. The film was awarded the "Audience Award for Comedy Film of the Year" at the 2000 The Comedy Festival (formerly known as the "US Comedy Arts Festival") and was nominated for the "Grand Jury Prize" at the Slamdance Film Festival the same year.', 'node_id': 'a93cf0ba-7d40-4f82-9c9b-3dcf73ddc946', 'score': 1.1941498517990112}], 'consistency_check': 'CONSISTENT', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'CONTRADICTION', 'response': 'CONTRADICTION'}, 'latency': 1.1446854434907436, 'vram_usage': 1.30615234375}
