eration Paperclip for more on post-WWII Allied collaboration with Nazis).', 'node_id': '68d616f8-ccfe-46fa-9889-f89c339ba183', 'score': 1.014282464981079}, {'text': 'space program. He worked within the U.S. Army and NASA, where he managed the development of several systems, including the Pershing missile and the Saturn V Moon rocket. In 1984, the U.S. Government investigated him for war crimes, and he agreed to renounce his United States citizenship and leave the U.S. in return for not being prosecuted.', 'node_id': '7e1a30ed-8b60-4313-a9ef-67e25cbb3055', 'score': 1.0602521896362305}, {'text': 'Upon his return to East Germany ten years later, he became a professor at the Humboldt University of Berlin and was president of the East German Academy of Sciences.', 'node_id': '49d37680-5955-4076-8d35-6942a62bda5e', 'score': 1.0990405082702637}], 'consistency_check': 'MISSING', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'NEUTRAL', 'response': 'NEUTRAL'}, 'latency': 0.7190433237701654, 'vram_usage': 1.51708984375}
