['Stacey Kent'] {'response': 'Stacey Kent is married to Jim Tomlinson and she released an album entitled "Raconte-moi" in 2010. This album was her first recorded in the French language and featured mostly songs by French writers, as well as songs from the Great American Songbook and Bossa Nova catalogue.', 'query': 'Who is married to Jim Tomlinson and released an album entitled Raconte-moi?', 'retrieved_context': [{'text': 'Stacey Kent is an American jazz singer. She is married to saxophonist Jim Tomlinson.', 'node_id': 'b4277048-1c27-4b7b-980b-9ef2701df932', 'score': 0.9357568025588989}, {'text': "Raconte-moi... is a 2010 album by jazz singer Stacey Kent. This was Kent's first album recorded in the French language and featured mostly songs by French writers as well as songs from the Great American Songbook and Bossa Nova catalogue.", 'node_id': '11effb33-3d23-4a70-a8a6-2e639acb63f0', 'score': 0.9856643676757812}, {'text': 'Jim Tomlinson is a British tenor saxophonist, clarinetist, producer, arranger and composer, born 9 September 1966, in Sutton Coldfield, Warwickshire, England.', 'node_id': 'd4c6d85b-da77-43d9-8e88-e5f17c7635c4', 'score': 0.9903287291526794}, {'text': 'As a solo musician, Hawley has released seven studio albums. He has been nominated for a Mercury prize twice and once for a Brit Award. He has collaborated with Lisa Marie Presley, Arctic Monkeys, Manic Street Preachers and Paul Weller.', 'node_id': '503c34fe-146e-488e-89a3-3c5a75ce4eb0', 'score': 1.0836714506149292}, {'text': 'Guitarist Jim Fairchild joined the band in 2009. The band\'s sixth album, "Strangers to Ourselves", was released on March 17, 2015.', 'node_id': '18ff4b18-3320-44f1-9c17-5efee72a8fa9', 'score': 1.1044692993164062}, {'text': 'She broke music career after releasing Çocuk ("Child" in Turkish) albüm in 1998 due to marrying with Zeki Aköz, who is her manager in 1996 and her disease, Aneurysm. She released fourth album, "Carpe Diem" ("Seize the day" in Latin), in 2006.', 'node_id': 'b54448e5-6a48-47c4-9a9d-5fc759b62d2e', 'score': 1.1513173580169678}, {'text': 'MacKaye is a member of The Evens, a two-piece indie rock group he formed with his wife Amy Farina in 2001.', 'node_id': '32882fa9-a8ad-47b6-a36d-05c3a62e9021', 'score': 1.1552467346191406}, {'text': 'The Raconteurs , also known as The Saboteurs in Australia, is an American rock supergroup that was formed in Detroit, Michigan, featuring four musicians associated with earlier musical projects: Jack White (formerly of The White Stripes, currently The Dead Weather, as well as solo), Brendan Benson (solo), Jack Lawrence (of The Greenhornes, Blanche and The Dead Weather), and Patrick Keeler (also of The Greenhornes).', 'node_id': '7672f97e-e89d-4420-af0a-c773e92cd571', 'score': 1.1754857301712036}, {'text': 'and "Come Again." Takahashi was also a member of Avex\'s 20th anniversary dance music project Ravex, and has produced songs for musicians such as Crystal Kay, Ami Suzuki and Rie Fu, and remixes for Hikaru Utada and Ayumi Hamasaki. He has formed the record labels Tachytelic Records and TCY Recording.', 'node_id': 'ed06c019-89a6-4407-900b-e3a1ff5b986d', 'score': 1.197664499282837}, {'text': 'Other collaborators have included Tom Rainey, Christian Lillinger, Ben Monder, Eivind Opsvik, Nasheet Waits, Samo Salamon and Michael Formanek. His first album as a co-leader was "Cosas" with Joey Sellers.', 'node_id': '0661a308-91eb-4ec7-8a45-ddcb5fa3e511', 'score': 1.2131695747375488}], 'consistency_check': 'CONSISTENT', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'ENTAILMENT', 'response': 'NEUTRAL'}, 'latency': 4.461355308070779, 'vram_usage': 1.23583984375}
