66632', 'score': 1.0953218936920166}, {'text': 'Joseph Hillis Miller Jr. (born March 5, 1928) is an American literary critic who has been heavily influenced by—and who has heavily influenced—deconstruction.', 'node_id': '5b687bf6-31e5-4fdd-a8ea-97b4f9e970ed', 'score': 1.1113502979278564}], 'consistency_check': 'MISSING', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'NEUTRAL', 'response': 'ENTAILMENT'}, 'latency': 1.3796411342918873, 'vram_usage': 1.14208984375}
