l American football player in the early National Football League and the first American Football League. He played for three pro teams over the course of two years. In 1926 he played with the Canton Bulldogs in the NFL and the Cleveland Panthers in the AFL. He played the following season with the NFL\'s Pottsville Maroons. Prior to his professional career, Roberts played college football for the Iowa State Cyclones.', 'node_id': '77102e36-940a-40e1-a8f6-71ae20a61cda', 'score': 1.0694714784622192}, {'text': "The 1988 Los Angeles Raiders season was the club's 29th season in the NFL. Mike Shanahan was hired as head coach, and the club finished with a 7–9 record. The Raiders drafted Heisman Trophy winner Tim Brown, making Brown the third person on the Raiders roster to have won the Heisman Trophy, the others being Marcus Allen and Bo Jackson. Most of the team's success throughout the season came through their division, as the Raiders finished 6-2 against the weak AFC West division, with their only 2 losses against the champions of the division, the Seattle Seahawks.", 'node_id': '98441378-c050-440d-97df-a4b2b6417ef2', 'score': 1.0760283470153809}], 'consistency_check': 'MISSING', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'ENTAILMENT', 'response': 'NEUTRAL'}, 'latency': 1.2841531075537205, 'vram_usage': 1.17724609375}
