['2,586'] {'response': 'The provided context is insufficient regarding the specific population of the nearby city that shares a zipcode with Hot Coffee, Mississippi at the 2010 census. The context mentions that Hot Coffee is sometimes assigned the same zipcode as nearby Collins, but it does not provide the population of Collins or any other nearby city at that census.', 'query': 'Hot Coffee, Mississippi sometimes shares a zipcode with a nearby city with what population at the 2010 census?', 'retrieved_context': [{'text': 'Hot Coffee is a locale in Covington County, Mississippi, celebrated in local Mississippi lore. It is sometimes assigned the same zipcode as nearby Collins.', 'node_id': '34155382-79ca-47da-99b7-30758929fd98', 'score': 0.7309551239013672}, {'text': 'The population was 301 at the 2011 census , and 103 in 2006.', 'node_id': '47c1c781-befc-463f-96a3-0e26cd5f711f', 'score': 1.241443157196045}, {'text': "According to the 2011 census, 62,888 people lived in the Cumberland portion of Orléans, while 44,935 people lived in the Gloucester portion. Today, Orléans spans the municipal wards of Orléans, Innes and Cumberland. Orléans is one of 3 areas of the post-amalgamated City of Ottawa to contain a significant francophone population, hence the community's name.", 'node_id': 'fcea11a7-b706-4d3a-ab6d-f30b92a8c19b', 'score': 1.2945952415466309}, {'text': 'The most populous city in the country is the capital, Mexico City, with a population of 8.9 million (2016), and its metropolitan area is also the most populated with 20.1 million (2010). Approximately 50% of the population lives in one of the 55 large metropolitan areas in the country. In total, about 78.84% of the population of the country lives in urban areas, meaning that only 21.16% live in rural areas.', 'node_id': 'af54de07-b855-4b1b-a8b7-e78370d9eefb', 'score': 1.3012216091156006}, {'text': 'At the 2011 Census this ward had a population of 16,099.', 'node_id': '302cff6a-305e-4506-95a1-da078d26a062', 'score': 1.3074439764022827}, {'text': 'As of 2014, the city had an estimated population of 91,196, up from 88,410 in 2010, making it the second most populous city in the county after Santa Maria while the contiguous urban area, which includes the cities of Goleta and Carpinteria, along with the unincorporated regions of Isla Vista, Montecito, Mission Canyon, Hope Ranch, Summerland, and others, has an approximate population of 220,000. The population of the entire county in 2010 was 423,895.', 'node_id': '6aaf2535-1926-4ff8-b627-4e57a6d7ac7a', 'score': 1.3198657035827637}, {'text': 'Part of Blennerville electoral division falls within the area of Tralee Town Council, and at the 2011 census had a population of 141. The remaining portion, outside the urban boundaries, had a 2011 population of 556.', 'node_id': '7a16b136-9246-43d0-9d32-d9e3fc4889c0', 'score': 1.3211489915847778}, {'text': '90 Church Street is a federal office building in Manhattan, New York City, New York, U.S. The building operates as the United States Postal Service\'s Church Street Station, which is responsible for the 10048 and 10007 ZIP codes. The building takes up a full block between Church Street and West Broadway and between Vesey and Barclay Streets in the Tribeca neighborhood of Manhattan. The "AIA Guide to New York City" says about the building: "A boring limestone monolith that has trouble deciding between a heritage of stripped down neo-Classical and a new breath of Art Deco."', 'node_id': '2c651866-7d63-4bb6-8658-e26f2b3c8175', 'score': 1.3213496208190918}, {'text': 'The Calumet Downtown Historic District is a historic district located in Calumet, Michigan, on 5th Street and 6th Street, between Scott Street and Pine Street. It is also known as the Red Jacket Downtown Historic District, reflecting the original name of the village. The Historic District is completely contained in the Calumet Historic District (a National Historic Landmark District) and the Keweenaw National Historical Park. It was designated a Michigan State Historic Site in 1973 and listed on the National Register of Historic Places in 1974.', 'node_id': '4f5aaffc-d667-4a03-9d65-b46bc605762e', 'score': 1.3596763610839844}, {'text': 'Quality Cafe is the name of two different former locations in Downtown Los Angeles, California.', 'node_id': '13efcadc-9543-4a5e-af1e-47b0ae0b6a42', 'score': 1.3706278800964355}], 'consistency_check': 'MISSING', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'ENTAILMENT', 'response': 'NEUTRAL'}, 'latency': 3.61696076951921, 'vram_usage': 1.27099609375}
