 77%|███████▋  | 383/500 [1:02:58<23:25, 12.01s/it]['Valley View Casino Center'] {'response': "The San Diego Gulls play their home games at the Valley View Casino Center, which is located at Sports Arena Blvd in Point Loma, San Diego. This arena serves as the venue for the Gulls' home games since the team began playing in the 2015–16 season.", 'query': 'The San Diego Gulls are a professional ice hockey team in the American Hockey League (AHL) which began playing in the 2015–16 season, the Gulls play their home games at which indoor arena located at Sports Arena Blvd in Point Loma, San Diego?', 'retrieved_context': [{'text': 'The San Diego Gulls are a professional ice hockey team in the American Hockey League (AHL) which began playing in the 2015–16 season. Based in San Diego, California and affiliated with the National Hockey League\'s Anaheim Ducks, the Gulls play their home games at the Valley View Casino Center. The team is the fifth hockey team in San Diego to use the "Gulls" name. The Gulls are a relocation of the former Norfolk Admirals (AHL) franchise, joining six other AHL franchises to form a new AHL Pacific Division.', 'node_id': 'cb434c45-889d-4f0f-8836-e4321b0930de', 'score': 0.1786656379699707}, {'text': 'The San Diego Gulls (1990–95) was a professional ice hockey team. The team, the second to use the "Gulls" nickname, was founded in 1990 as part of the International Hockey League. The Gulls played at the San Diego Sports Arena.', 'node_id': '097bbcc5-256c-4d78-a47b-3c68be994034', 'score': 0.2524891495704651}, {'text': 'The San Diego Gulls were a professional ice hockey team in the West Coast Hockey League (WCHL) and later in the ECHL. The team, the third to use the "Gulls" nickname, was founded in 1995 immediately upon the departure of the IHL team of the same name. The Gulls played at the San Diego Sports Arena.', 'node_id': 'bc1a90d3-82ea-4fca-8f21-419b69760842', 'score': 0.274199903011322}, {'text': 'The original San Diego Gulls team was founded in 1966 as part of the Western Hockey League. The Gulls played at the San Diego Sports Arena.', 'node_id': '2e21c07c-cebb-4749-877c-fe4ef1bc80fa', 'score': 0.3514932692050934}, {'text': 'The San Diego Sabers are a junior ice hockey team. They are a member of the Western Division in the Western States Hockey League based in Escondido, California and plays at the Iceoplex-Escondido. The team was the fourth team to be known as the San Diego Gulls from 2008 to 2015 until it gave up the nickname to the American Hockey League San Diego Gulls before the 2015–16 season.', 'node_id': 'b49c9f9c-2ea7-496d-b8fa-ab2a16b8b1c7', 'score': 0.5749669075012207}], 'consistency_check': 'CONSISTENT', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'CONTRADICTION', 'response': 'CONTRADICTION'}, 'latency': 0.9972337260842323, 'vram_usage': 1.66943359375}
