['August Burns Red'] {'response': 'The producer of "The Wreckage of Stars," which is the debut full-length album by the progressive death metal band Black Crown Initiate, is Carson Slovak. According to the provided context, he has also produced albums for Texas in July and Everclear. Additionally, there is mention of another American metalcore band from Lancaster, Pennsylvania, which is This or the Apocalypse. Therefore, the answer to the question is that the producer Carson Slovak also worked with This or the Apocalypse, another American metalcore band from Lancaster, Pennsylvania.', 'query': 'The producer of The Wreckage of Stars also produced albums for Texas in July, Everclear, and what other American metalcore band from Lancaster, Pennsylvania?', 'retrieved_context': [{'text': 'Texas in July was an American metalcore band from Ephrata, Pennsylvania, formed in 2007. They released an EP, "Salt of the Earth", and their debut full-length album, "I Am", through CI Records. After signing with Equal Vision Records, they released three more studio albums: "One Reality" on April 26, 2011; a self-titled album on October 9, 2012; and finally "Bloodwork" on September 16, 2014. The band broke up at the end of 2015.', 'node_id': '047c0298-60db-408a-a88e-44df86ccc311', 'score': 0.8165587186813354}, {'text': 'The Wreckage of Stars is the debut full length record from American based progressive death metal band Black Crown Initiate. The album was released on September 30, 2014 through eOne Music and was produced by Carson Slovak (August Burns Red, Texas In July, Everclear). A music video was filmed for "Withering Waves" and "The Fractured One". The album debuted at #18 on the Billboard Heatseekers chart.', 'node_id': '0a919924-f879-4fc7-9e1a-182fe591cf55', 'score': 0.8470098376274109}, {'text': 'This or the Apocalypse is an American metalcore band from Lancaster, Pennsylvania which formed in 2005.', 'node_id': '69a146d2-a7a9-4769-8cb6-cba2ea2c31ba', 'score': 0.8774476051330566}, {'text': "Metallica is an American heavy metal band based in San Rafael, California. The band was formed in 1981 in Los Angeles when vocalist/guitarist James Hetfield responded to an advertisement posted by drummer Lars Ulrich in a local newspaper. Metallica's current lineup comprises founding members Hetfield and Ulrich, longtime lead guitarist Kirk Hammett, and bassist Robert Trujillo. Guitarist Dave Mustaine (who went on to form Megadeth) and bassists Ron McGovney, Cliff Burton, and Jason Newsted are also former members of the band.", 'node_id': 'a47faf43-f8e4-4902-9c97-92721434c947', 'score': 1.114210605621338}, {'text': 'Far away from renouncing to their genre, they have always claimed that they were a heavy metal band and they even wrote a song about this genre in their first LP called"Dosis de Heavy Metal".In 2012, because of their 30th anniversary, they did a Tour around Spain.', 'node_id': '4453416a-db8a-4246-a06f-5c1fb9f90da1', 'score': 1.124786138534546}], 'consistency_check': 'CONSISTENT', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'NEUTRAL', 'response': 'ENTAILMENT'}, 'latency': 1.5912115778774023, 'vram_usage': 1.38818359375}
