['John Carney'] {'response': 'The provided context is insufficient regarding who directed a 2016 musical filmed in Howth. While it mentions several films and their directors, it does not specify any 2016 musical that was filmed in Howth or provide information about the director of such a film.', 'query': 'Who directed a 2016 musical filmed in Howth?', 'retrieved_context': [{'text': 'Howth has been a filming location for movies such as "The Last of the High Kings", "Boy Eats Girl" and "Sing Street".', 'node_id': 'a9bb5538-363d-4faf-ab40-5e2bed4ff81a', 'score': 5.979608535766602}, {'text': 'And You Were Wonderful, On Stage is a 2016 musical film written and directed by Cally Spooner and starring Rhiannon Drake, Jenny Minton, Piya Malik, Rebecca Thorn and Chloë Turpin. The film is based on the performance artwork of the same name, which toured internationally from 2013-15. It premiered at the Stedelijk Museum on 15 January 2016. The piece is delivered by a chorus line of women, who gossip about celebrities and the media, with text based on notes from a meeting of an advertising agency.', 'node_id': '105a9833-91fd-4c7f-a31b-c74ffa13183b', 'score': 5.297954559326172}, {'text': 'Fred Berger (born May 10, 1981) is an American film producer who was nominated for the Academy Award for Best Picture for the 2016 musical "La La Land", for which he also won the 2016 Golden Globe Award for Best Motion Picture – Musical or Comedy and Producers Guild of America Award for Best Theatrical Motion Picture.', 'node_id': '219cbe46-1ea1-496b-b711-0b2e10bd8708', 'score': 5.130348205566406}, {'text': 'Little Shop of Horrors is a 1986 American rock musical horror comedy film directed by Frank Oz. It is a film adaptation of the off-Broadway musical comedy of the same name by composer Alan Menken and writer Howard Ashman about a nerdy florist shop worker who finds out his venus fly trap can speak. Menken and Ashman\'s Off-Broadway musical was based on the low-budget 1960 film "The Little Shop of Horrors", directed by Roger Corman.', 'node_id': '0f186337-8d61-4ec3-8374-cfe3142325e4', 'score': 4.884641647338867}, {'text': 'Insane (, "Come to see Me") is a 2016 South Korean thriller film directed by Lee Cheol-ha. It was released in South Korea on April 7, 2016.', 'node_id': 'c0a96117-a6ce-4719-8417-5631941eaa6d', 'score': 4.865795612335205}, {'text': "Kristin Chenoweth: My Love Letter to Broadway is a 2016 musical revue / concert, written for and starring American singer and actress Kristin Chenoweth. The show was directed by Richard Jay-Alexander, with musical direction by Mary Mitchell Campbell, and produced by James L. Nederlander. The show was a limited engagement of 12 performances at Broadway's Lunt-Fontanne Theatre from November 2 through 13, 2016.", 'node_id': '071c2cbb-0c28-493f-bd8a-476fc49162a6', 'score': 4.824122905731201}, {'text': 'Seoul Station (Korean: 서울역 ) is a South Korean animated zombie drama film written and directed by Yeon Sang-ho. Released on August 18, 2016, the film stars Ryu Seung-ryong, Shim Eun-kyung and Lee Joon in the lead roles. The film was shown at the 2016 Edinburgh International Film Festival.', 'node_id': 'c064ff5c-fc16-4516-8270-a382a3cb044e', 'score': 4.575441360473633}, {'text': 'The film was co-directed by Bob Peterson, with music composed by Michael Giacchino.', 'node_id': 'd023cdc3-e6d0-467d-951c-4178fb544f4f', 'score': 4.446246147155762}, {'text': 'Lovesick is a Canadian romantic comedy film, released in 2016. It was written and directed by Winnipeg filmmaker Tyson Caron, his directorial debut.', 'node_id': 'bafdf2ec-b08b-486b-ae56-7e7eb750509d', 'score': 4.442538261413574}, {'text': 'Yeon Sang-ho (born 1978) is a South Korean film director and screenwriter. He wrote and directed the animated films "The King of Pigs" (2011) and "The Fake" (2013), and the live-action film "Train to Busan" (2016).', 'node_id': '4e5c3a0c-a49f-4782-bdbe-2927fced9e03', 'score': 4.372812747955322}], 'consistency_check': 'MISSING', 'ent