['Prodigy'] {'response': 'The provided context is insufficient regarding which guest who appeared in the album "Animal Ambition" was born with the name Albert Johnson.', 'query': 'Which guest who appeared in the album "Animal Ambition" was born with the name Albert Johnson? ', 'retrieved_context': [{'text': 'Albert Johnson (November 2, 1974 – June 20, 2017), better known by his stage name Prodigy, was an American rapper, actor and author who was one half of the hip hop duo Mobb Deep with Havoc.', 'node_id': '630fb409-e241-4597-a18e-f86cb72e22cf', 'score': 0.9538300037384033}, {'text': 'Albert M. Johnson (November 18, 1900 - September 18, 1966) was an American Hall of Fame jockey. Born in the rural community of Milan, Washington, Albert Johnson began his career in 1917 at Playfair Race Track in nearby Spokane. His success at local racetracks led to a move to tracks in the New York City area where he was the principal jockey for Morvich in his undefeated two-year-old season in 1921 and with whom he won the 1922 Kentucky Derby.', 'node_id': '70de4ea3-09a7-4fe5-82ed-d5143dc38c2c', 'score': 1.0290093421936035}, {'text': 'Animal Ambition (released with the subtitle Animal Ambition: An Untamed Desire to Win) is the fifth studio album by American rapper 50 Cent, who also served as executive producer. The album was released on June 3, 2014, by G-Unit Records and Caroline Records.', 'node_id': 'ed3c726a-232a-4544-b00b-ac38bbd836c6', 'score': 1.0862646102905273}, {'text': 'Albert Johnson (died February 17, 1932), known as the Mad Trapper of Rat River, was a fugitive whose actions eventually sparked off a huge manhunt in the Northwest Territories and Yukon in Northern Canada. The event became a media circus as Johnson eluded the Royal Canadian Mounted Police (RCMP) team sent to take him into custody, which ended after a 150 mi foot chase lasting more than a month and a shootout in which Johnson was fatally wounded on the Eagle River, Yukon. Albert Johnson was a pseudonym and his true identity remains unknown.', 'node_id': 'e990c06f-d3e2-4026-8ae8-a92b5ed3d6f3', 'score': 1.1709195375442505}, {'text': "Albert Johnson III (born November 11, 1977 in Houston, Texas) is a Canadian Football League player for the Winnipeg Blue Bombers. Johnson played his college football for Southern Methodist University and then signed with the Saskatchewan Roughriders where he played three games in 1999. Johnson then signed with the Blue Bombers and went on to win the league's Rookie of the Year Award in 2000 after leading the league in return yardage. He signed with the Texans]] but suffered injuries throughout his National Football League stint.", 'node_id': '23a18d77-dde1-4706-8789-bd1ddbc92278', 'score': 1.1830940246582031}], 'consistency_check': 'CONFLICT', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'CONTRADICTION', 'response': 'ENTAILMENT'}, 'latency': 0.7547521088272333, 'vram_usage': 1.24755859375}
