 83%|████████▎ | 413/500 [1:07:44<11:48,  8.15s/it]['Dirt'] {'response': '"Hate to Feel" is the tenth track on Alice in Chains\' album "Dirt," which was released on September 29, 1992. The album "Dirt" peaked at number six on the Billboard 200 chart and is notable for being the band\'s highest selling album to date, having been certified four-times platinum by the RIAA and selling five million copies worldwide.', 'query': "Hate to Feel is the tenth track on what Alice in Chains' album that peaked as number six on the Billboard 200?", 'retrieved_context': [{'text': '"Hate to Feel" is the tenth track on Alice in Chains\' album "Dirt" (1992). The song was included on the compilation albums "Music Bank" (1999) and "The Essential Alice in Chains". It has also been the ninth track on later prints of the album and eleventh on others. Some editions of "Dirt" may merge this song with the then-unlisted 43-second track "Iron Gland".', 'node_id': '10ba6083-9a5a-4684-ab5c-23d19588d7ea', 'score': 0.47165125608444214}, {'text': 'Dirt is the second studio album by the American rock band Alice in Chains, released on September 29, 1992, through Columbia Records. Peaking at number six on the "Billboard" 200, the album was also well received by music critics. It has since been certified four-times platinum by the RIAA and gone on to sell five million copies worldwide, making "Dirt" the band\'s highest selling album to date. It is the band\'s last album recorded with all four original members, as bassist Mike Starr was terminated from the band in January 1993.', 'node_id': '3d99103a-9346-4ffe-9ca4-b01f06ebbcf8', 'score': 0.8647935390472412}, {'text': 'It peaked at number 6 on the U.S. "Billboard" Hot Country Singles & Tracks chart and at number 7 on the Canadian "RPM" Country Tracks chart.', 'node_id': '15c3df41-651a-4679-ac3f-69ce9cc05ec0', 'score': 1.007379412651062}, {'text': "The album debuted #1 on the ear X-tacy sales chart, #92 on the CIMS sales chart, #20 on R&R's specialty chart, and #7 on FMQB's Submodern Report.", 'node_id': 'ae9e46bc-ef90-4041-9404-cf8c2afd4376', 'score': 1.0459306240081787}, {'text': 'In the US, the track reached number 59 on the "Billboard" Hot 100 singles chart, becoming the band\'s second single to hit the chart after "There\'s No Other Way". It also reached number 4 on the Modern Rock songs chart.', 'node_id': '55c8d85b-6775-4842-bc23-72a252ffa8b7', 'score': 1.0482990741729736}], 'consistency_check': 'MISSING', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'NEUTRAL', 'response': 'NEUTRAL'}, 'latency': 1.318019237369299, 'vram_usage': 1.30615234375}
