['yes'] {'response': "Yes, both Tim McIlrath and Spike Slawson are American punk rock musicians. Tim McIlrath is known as the lead singer, rhythm guitarist, songwriter, and co-founder of the American punk rock band Rise Against, while Spike Slawson is a member of several punk rock bands, including Me First and the Gimme Gimmes and Swingin' Utters. Their contributions to the punk rock genre highlight their significance within the American music scene.", 'query': 'Are both Tim McIlrath and Spike Slawson American punk rock musicians?', 'retrieved_context': [{'text': "Spike Slawson is an American punk rock musician, a member of Me First and the Gimme Gimmes, Swingin' Utters, Filthy Thievin' Bastards, Re-Volts, and Uke-Hunt.", 'node_id': 'cb9be768-a3bc-430f-a598-8a5c25bbdf58', 'score': 0.7696898579597473}, {'text': 'Timothy James "Tim" McIlrath (born November 3, 1978) is an American punk rock musician. He is the lead singer, rhythm guitarist, songwriter and co-founder of the American punk rock band Rise Against. McIlrath is known to support animal rights and actively promotes PETA with his band. He is also straight edge.', 'node_id': '4908eef9-445d-4a16-bd5b-764587035873', 'score': 0.8832041621208191}, {'text': "The current lineup consists of Jonathan Balzano-Brookes (vocals, guitar), Tim Burns (guitar, vocals), Joe Domrad (drums), Jacob Chamberlain (drums), Sean Newton (bass), and Philip Willey (guitar, accordion, keyboards). The band has released music domestically on the Time-Lag Records label and in the UK on Rough Trade Records. The band's jangly, psychedelic pop music has been compared to The Byrds and New Zealand's The Chills, as well as North American indie-pop acts like The Shins and The New Pornographers.", 'node_id': '534a5c1d-775a-40b7-8021-e166f84718ea', 'score': 1.0250831842422485}, {'text': 'The Raconteurs , also known as The Saboteurs in Australia, is an American rock supergroup that was formed in Detroit, Michigan, featuring four musicians associated with earlier musical projects: Jack White (formerly of The White Stripes, currently The Dead Weather, as well as solo), Brendan Benson (solo), Jack Lawrence (of The Greenhornes, Blanche and The Dead Weather), and Patrick Keeler (also of The Greenhornes).', 'node_id': '7672f97e-e89d-4420-af0a-c773e92cd571', 'score': 1.0433225631713867}, {'text': 'Timothy Robert "Tim" Maurer (born October 10, 1980) is an American singer, best known as the former lead singer of third-wave ska band Suburban Legends. He has left the band on two separate occasions. The first was in 2000 after the recording of Origin Edition. He rejoined the band in early 2002 after his replacement singer Chris Batstone left the band. He officially left the band again in September 2005 after the band\'s third consecutive appearance on the Jerry Lewis MDA Telethon, performing a new song entitled "Moving Closer."', 'node_id': 'c6475c06-d3f5-4cd0-ac79-983d8b396d5e', 'score': 1.070578694343567}, {'text': 'They drew influences from early 1980s hardcore punk bands such as Minor Threat, Flipper and Bad Brains, as well as more recent noise and indie rock bands such as Lightning Bolt, Fugazi, and Shellac, and math rock bands including Hella and Don Caballero.', 'node_id': '13e4fa95-60aa-4df8-9469-0ea516aa1bfe', 'score': 1.0764529705047607}, {'text': 'Vincent Francis Walker (born March 2, 1980), better known as Vince Walker, is an American multi-instrumentalist, best known as the lead singer of third-wave ska band Suburban Legends. He was formerly the lead trumpet player, and left sometime after the release of "Rump Shaker", but returned to the band in September 2005 for the band\'s appearance on the Jerry Lewis MDA Telethon, which happened to be lead singer Tim Maurer\'s last performance. He replaced Maurer as the singer in an odd switching of roles, and continues with the band as frontman.', 'node_id': '0974ba5a-e8b2-4d10-bea3-7e8e184f5b99', 'score': 1.0897207260131836}, {'text': 'The Playbills, which describe the musical as having "explosions, negligible storytelling, camouflage and tits", also state that the musical\'s cast included actors such as Taye Diggs (who would go on to play the role of Hedwig in the summer of 2015) and that the music was written by Metallica and Stephen R. Schwartz, which is the real name of "Hedwig" songwriter Stephen Trask.', 'node_id': 'e1f4a03f-f9f6-40e7-8bf9-9549402abbb9', 'score': 1.098059892654419}, {'text': 'Brian Robertson (born October 19, 1979) is the trombone player for the Orange County-based third-wave ska band Suburban Legends and, along with Vincent Walker, is one of the two members to have played with the band since its origin as Bomb Squad. He met other ex-Suburban Legends / Bomb Squad members, trumpet player Aaron Bertram and best friend and trombone player Ryan Dallas Cook through the Huntington Beach High School Marching Band.', 'node_id': '441722c5-0926-44b6-8175-1cd328b991de', 'score': 1.1274981498718262}, {'text': 'Nathan Jonas "Joey" Jordison (born April 26, 1975), is an American musician, songwriter, record producer and multi-instrumentalist, best known for his work as the former drummer and co-songwriter for the American heavy metal band Slipknot as well as guitarist in the American horror punk band Murderdolls. Jordison played in Slipknot since their formation in 1995 until his departure from the band in December 2013.', 'node_id': '85f61e14-ceab-4915-a8eb-6647b50adf6d', 'score': 1.1391010284423828}], 'consistency_check': 'MISSING', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'ENTAILMENT', 'response': 'ENTAILMENT'}, 'latency': 1.3259653989225626, 'vram_usage': 1.21240234375}
