 87%|████████▋ | 437/500 [1:13:00<11:37, 11.08s/it] 88%|████████▊ | 438/500 [1:13:05<09:29,  9.18s/it] 88%|████████▊ | 439/500 [1:13:21<11:35, 11.40s/it] 88%|████████▊ | 440/500 [1:13:33<11:30, 11.51s/it] 88%|████████▊ | 441/500 [1:13:43<10:53, 11.07s/it]['Neosho River'] {'response': 'The provided context is insufficient regarding the specific river along which Emprise Bank has branches in a city.', 'query': 'Emprise Bank has branches in a city situated along what river?', 'retrieved_context': [{'text': 'Emprise Bank is a Kansas-based, family owned, community bank headquartered in Wichita, Kansas with more than $1 billion in assets. Emprise has 37 locations across the state of Kansas, including branches in Wichita, Andover, Augusta, Chanute, Clearwater, Council Grove, Derby, El Dorado, Eureka, Goddard, Hays, Haysville, Hillsboro, Humboldt, Iola, Lawrence, McPherson, Moran, Mulvane, Park City, Potwin, Rose Hill, and Valley Center.', 'node_id': '4fdba766-06bb-40d2-9a8b-73be09f5cce8', 'score': 0.9043075442314148}, {'text': '1st Valley Bank is a development bank (3rd in terms of assets) in the Philippines, based in Baroy, Lanao del Norte and servicing various areas in Mindanao, specifically the provinces of Lanao del Norte, Lanao del Sur, Misamis Occidental, Misamis Oriental, Bukidnon, Zamboanga del Norte, Zamboanga del Sur and Zamboanga Sibugay.', 'node_id': '3d8ac7e2-cf4d-41d0-87dc-b7e7d1bed3e6', 'score': 1.0585359334945679}, {'text': 'The islet is linked to both banks of the river by bridges and the castle has now been converted into a small hotel. Bradt Travel Guides calls it "one of the most famous hotels in Slovenia."', 'node_id': 'e78af725-b244-437a-8dc1-6350c6c6510d', 'score': 1.1735111474990845}, {'text': 'Primarily running along its namesake street, Canal Street, it consists of two branches named for their outer terminals, totaling about 5+1/2 mi in length: "Canal - Cemeteries" (officially designated as Route 47) and "Canal - City Park/Museum" (officially designated as Route 48). Each branch is denoted with the red and light green colors respectively on most RTA publications.', 'node_id': 'c3a264fa-feba-41a4-b38c-f7978df90c15', 'score': 1.1931705474853516}, {'text': 'The River is a 1984 American drama film directed by Mark Rydell, written by Robert Dillon and Julian Barry, and stars Mel Gibson, Sissy Spacek, and Scott Glenn. The film tells the story of a struggling farm family in the Tennessee valley trying to keep its farm from going under in the face of bank foreclosures and floods. The father faces the dilemma of having to work as a strikebreaker in a steel mill to keep his family farm from foreclosure. It was based on the true story of farmers who unknowingly took jobs as strikebreakers at a steel mill after their crops had been destroyed by rain.', 'node_id': 'd0871011-5705-41e5-944d-7574b7d883a4', 'score': 1.244546890258789}], 'consistency_check': 'CONFLICT', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'NEUTRAL', 'response': 'CONTRADICTION'}, 'latency': 0.6949987299740314, 'vram_usage': 1.18896484375}
