, Victoria who often collaborated with his brothers Charles and John.', 'node_id': '4ad31047-2467-48a5-bec1-f00d5d312249', 'score': 1.2182872295379639}, {'text': "Senator; Charles Lee, U.S. Supreme Court justice; Richard Bland Lee II, a noted explorer; Robert E. Lee, the Confederate general who is by far the most famous of the family; William Henry Fitzhugh (Rooney) Lee, the son of Robert E. Lee and a U.S. Congressman from Virginia; and Fitzhugh Lee, Governor of Virginia and Civil War cavalry general. President Zachary Taylor was a Lee descendant, on his mother's side.", 'node_id': 'd49aa7f2-b7af-4ed4-a929-4887b1b38337', 'score': 1.223374605178833}], 'consistency_check': 'MISSING', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'CONTRADICTION', 'response': 'NEUTRAL'}, 'latency': 0.7587128672748804, 'vram_usage': 1.13037109375}
