 99%|█████████▊| 493/500 [1:21:59<01:11, 10.18s/it] 99%|█████████▉| 494/500 [1:22:03<00:48,  8.14s/it]['International Association of Machinists'] {'response': "The airline founded by Frank Lorenzo that was affected by a strike in 1989 was Eastern Air Lines. Charlie Bryan, who was the head of the International Association of Machinists union in the southeast United States, led machinists to strike against Eastern Air Lines and Frank Lorenzo during that time. This strike was a significant event in the airline's history and highlighted the tensions between labor unions and management in the airline industry during the late 1980s.", 'query': 'Which airline founded by Frank Lorenzo was affected by a strike in 1989?', 'retrieved_context': [{'text': 'Francisco Anthony "Frank" Lorenzo (born May 19, 1940) is an American businessman and philanthropist. He is most famous for his leadership of Texas International Airlines and its successor holding company Texas Air Corporation between 1972 and 1990, through which he formed or acquired a number of major U.S. airlines including Continental Airlines, Eastern Air Lines, Frontier Airlines, New York Air and People Express Airlines.', 'node_id': '9ad209e5-a65c-4bf7-b684-259cdc3aaeb4', 'score': 0.6517767906188965}, {'text': 'Ryan Airline Company was an airline founded by T. Claude Ryan and Benjamin Franklin "Frank" Mahoney at San Diego, California on April 19, 1925. They had earlier established a scheduled service between San Diego and Los Angeles with a fare of $14.50 one-way and $22.50 round-trip.', 'node_id': 'e86a9ec6-1232-48f1-8d6f-c79c283e98af', 'score': 0.9296708106994629}, {'text': 'Air Caribbean was an airline that served from Luis Muñoz Marín International Airport, then "Isla Verde International Airport", in San Juan. The 1970s and 1980s were decades when several Puerto Rican airlines existed and competed against each other, including Prinair, Vieques Air Link and Dorado Wings. Believing a share of the market profits could be gained, Air Caribbean was created in 1975.', 'node_id': '25c46c0d-5b91-43ab-9d2a-919adfc3b085', 'score': 1.0302331447601318}, {'text': 'Fina Air was an airline based in San Juan, Puerto Rico named after Josefina Canto who was the mother of Lazaro Canto. It operated charter flights to the Dominican Republic from Luis Muñoz Marín International Airport in San Juan, Rafael Hernández Airport in Aguadilla and Eugenio María de Hostos Airport in Mayagüez. The airline has now ceased operations.', 'node_id': '0d23beb8-60b9-4690-93f6-edf6745966a1', 'score': 1.13124418258667}, {'text': 'Charlie Bryan (11 December 1933 - 2 November 2013) was the head of the International Association of Machinists union in the southeast United States, during the mid to late 1980s. He led machinists to strike against Eastern Air Lines and Frank Lorenzo in 1989.', 'node_id': 'a5a88f9c-5c19-4ee5-ab42-2ae39df61d4c', 'score': 1.1331067085266113}], 'consistency_check': 'MISSING', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'ENTAILMENT', 'response': 'NEUTRAL'}, 'latency': 1.5162282083183527, 'vram_usage': 1.18896484375}
