 99%|█████████▉| 496/500 [1:22:30<00:45, 11.36s/it]['Tommy Morrison'] {'response': 'In the film "Rocky V," Michael Anthony Williams acted alongside real-life boxer Tommy Morrison. Morrison portrayed the character Tommy Gunn, a talented yet raw boxer, while Williams played the fictional boxer Union Cane. Their performances contributed to the film\'s exploration of boxing and the relationships within the sport.', 'query': 'What other real life boxer did Mike Williams act with in Rocky V?', 'retrieved_context': [{'text': 'Michael Anthony Williams (born June 16, 1962) is an American actor and former professional boxer who competed from 1984 to 2000. He is most notable for portraying fictional boxer Union Cane in the 1990 film "Rocky V".', 'node_id': 'd7c82ba9-7218-495e-9b94-a6aae1725fc7', 'score': 0.38518190383911133}, {'text': 'Tommy David Morrison (January 2, 1969 – September 1, 2013) was an American professional boxer who competed from 1988 to 1996, and held the WBO heavyweight title in 1993. He retired from boxing in 1996 when he tested positive for HIV, but returned for two more fights in 2007 and 2008. Morrison is also known for starring alongside Sylvester Stallone in the 1990 film "Rocky V".', 'node_id': '508ece2d-05c6-44ee-89b5-678fbbda3550', 'score': 0.6629581451416016}, {'text': 'Rocky V is a 1990 American sports drama film. It is the fifth film in the "Rocky" series, written by and starring Sylvester Stallone, and co-starring Talia Shire, Stallone\'s real-life son Sage, and real-life boxer Tommy Morrison, with Morrison in the role of Tommy Gunn, a talented yet raw boxer. Sage played Robert Balboa, whose relationship with his famous father is explored.', 'node_id': 'b9a94f68-5aff-4089-9b1d-e3bc4f559e0d', 'score': 0.7798731923103333}, {'text': "Mike McNulty (1887 - 1965) was an old time, old style and old method boxing manager and trainer, who managed and trained several world champion boxers during the first half of the 20th century, including Mike O'Dowd, Johnny Ertel, Mike Gibbons and, also, trained Mike’s brother Tommy Gibbons, the Ring Boxing and International Boxing Hall of Fame. In 1965, Mike McNulty died at Studio City Convalescent Hospital in Studio City, California at the age of 78.", 'node_id': '36f9ea06-b157-4ca2-8a00-6aeeb8e70540', 'score': 0.9614182710647583}, {'text': "Mike Gibbons (July 20, 1887 in St. Paul, Minnesota – August 31, 1956) was an American boxer from 1908 to 1922. The brother of heavyweight Tommy Gibbons, Mike claimed Middleweight Champion of the World status in 1909 following Stanley Ketchel's murder. Although he never won the title, Gibbons is regarded as one of the all-time best welter and middleweight boxers by historians.", 'node_id': '458c095c-ebce-468d-b0e0-bc20e7de7eda', 'score': 0.980975329875946}], 'consistency_check': 'CONSISTENT', 'entailment_check': {'query': 'CONTRADICTION', 'response': 'CONTRADICTION'}, 'latency': 1.0542479008436203, 'vram_usage': 1.18896484375}
